    <bpmn:process id="W_W562" name="W562. Store-Level Loss Prevention Daily Routine" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Store opening (LP daily checklist initiation)
Frequency: Daily at all 200 stores
Volume: 200 daily checklists completed
Owner: LP Officer / Store Manager (stores without dedicated LP Officer)
Participants: LP Officer, Store Manager, Cashiers (C), Stock Associates (C)
Source: workflow W562 — Store-Level Loss Prevention Daily Routine</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W562_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W562_Lane1" name="LP Officer">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W562_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W562_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W562_Task16</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W562_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W562_Lane2" name="Store Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W562_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W562_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W562_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W562_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W562_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W562_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W562_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W562_Task14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W562_Task15</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W562_End17</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W562_Start4" name="Store opening (LP daily checklist initiation)">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W562_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W562_Task5" name="LP Officer opens LP dashboard on tablet at store opening">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: LP Officer opens LP dashboard on tablet at store opening: LP Officer (or Store Manager on non-visit days) logs into LP module on tablet; dashboard displays: (a) today&#x27;s checklist items, (b) overnight exception alerts from W538 (voids, no-sales, refund patterns, sweet-hearting indicators), (c) pending investigation items from W248, (d) previous day&#x27;s checklist completion status; Officer acknowledges dashboard and begins daily routine
Responsible (R): LP Officer / Store Manager
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 5 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W562_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W562_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W562_Task6" name="EAS gate power-on test and functionality verification">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: EAS gate power-on test and functionality verification: at each store entrance/exit with EAS (Electronic Article Surveillance) gates: (a) power on EAS system, (b) test each gate with test tag (walk through with tagged item — verify alarm triggers), (c) test deactivation pad at POS (scan tagged item through — verify alarm does NOT trigger), (d) record pass/fail per gate in checklist; if gate fails: log maintenance request via W47, implement manual bag-check procedure for affected entrance until repaired
Responsible (R): Store Manager
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 5–10 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W562_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W562_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W562_Task7" name="High-value product cage/locked display integrity check">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: High-value product cage/locked display integrity check: verify security of high-value merchandise: (a) power tool cage — verify lock engaged, key accounted for, inventory count matches expected (spot-check 5 items against system), (b) locked display cases (premium appliances, high-end power tools, specialty hardware) — verify locks engaged, glass intact, item count correct, (c) key log review — verify all high-value key sign-outs from prior day are returned and logged; discrepancies flagged for immediate investigation per W248
Responsible (R): Store Manager
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 10–15 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W562_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W562_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W562_Task8" name="Review overnight exception alerts from W538">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Review overnight exception alerts from W538: review POS exception alerts generated overnight and from previous evening: (a) high-value voids (void &gt; PHP 5,000 after 8 PM), (b) excessive no-sale drawer opens (&gt; 3 per cashier per shift), (c) refund patterns (same cashier processing multiple refunds), (d) sweet-hearting indicators (repeated small-quantity scans of expensive items), (e) employee discount abuse patterns; prioritize alerts for follow-up investigation; flag top 3 alerts for Cashier performance discussion (W522)
Responsible (R): Store Manager
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 10–15 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W562_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W562_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W562_Task9" name="Check CCTV camera coverage — verify all cameras online">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Check CCTV camera coverage — verify all cameras online: access CCTV system (W71); verify all cameras showing live feed: (a) entrance/exit cameras, (b) POS lane cameras, (c) backroom/receiving door cameras, (d) high-value product cage camera, (e) parking lot cameras; for any offline cameras: log IT helpdesk ticket per W48 with priority &quot;Security System&quot;; document offline camera locations and estimated blind-spot coverage gap; adjust physical patrol frequency for areas with offline cameras
Responsible (R): Store Manager
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 5–10 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W562_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W562_Flow25</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W562_Task10" name="Blind-spot walkthrough — areas not covered by CCTV">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Blind-spot walkthrough — areas not covered by CCTV: walk areas with known CCTV blind spots: (a) restrooms and vestibule areas, (b) fitting/trial areas for workwear/PPE, (c) lumber yard corners and behind rack structures, (d) garden center rear sections, (e) receiving dock when not in active DSD receiving; look for: concealed merchandise, discarded packaging (evidence of in-store consumption or tag-switching), unauthorized access points; document observations in checklist
Responsible (R): Store Manager
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 10–15 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W562_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W562_Flow26</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W562_Task11" name="Fitting area / trial room check">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Fitting area / trial room check: verify fitting area procedures: (a) item count sign-in/sign-out board compliance — are associates counting items in and out?, (b) check trial rooms for concealed merchandise or discarded security tags, (c) verify EAS-detag only happens at POS (not in fitting area), (d) assess whether fitting area associate is actively monitoring; document compliance level
Responsible (R): Store Manager
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 5 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W562_Flow26</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W562_Flow27</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W562_Task12" name="DSD receiving observation — spot-check vendor deliveries">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 8: DSD receiving observation — spot-check vendor deliveries: if DSD receiving is occurring during visit: observe 1–2 deliveries per W18 for: (a) vendor identification verification, (b) item count vs. delivery receipt match, (c) quality inspection compliance, (d) short-shipment indicators (seal intact but count low, substitution without authorization), (e) vendor access restricted to receiving area only; if irregularities observed: escalate per W248 investigation protocol
Responsible (R): Store Manager
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 10–15 min (if DSD occurring)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W562_Flow27</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W562_Flow28</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W562_Task13" name="Mid-day till spot-check on 1 cashier">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 9: Mid-day till spot-check on 1 cashier: select 1 cashier for unannounced till spot-check: (a) pause cashier&#x27;s current transaction, (b) perform cash count of drawer, (c) compare physical cash to system expected amount per POS cash tracking, (d) variance &gt; PHP 200 (over or short): document per W272 cashier over/short protocol, (e) variance within tolerance: record as &quot;Pass&quot; in checklist; rotate cashier selection daily to cover all cashiers within 2-week cycle
Responsible (R): LP Officer / Store Manager
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 5–10 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W562_Flow28</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W562_Flow29</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W562_Task14" name="Afternoon high-value shelf count spot-check">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 10: Afternoon high-value shelf count spot-check: select 5–10 high-value SKUs from tools/hardware department: (a) physically count shelf and backroom quantity, (b) compare to system perpetual inventory (INV-001), (c) variance &gt; 2 units: flag for W248 inventory variance investigation, (d) look for evidence of tag-switching (wrong barcode on high-value item), (e) verify EAS tags present on all items requiring tagging; SKU selection varied daily to cover top 100 high-value SKUs within monthly cycle
Responsible (R): Store Manager
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 10–15 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W562_Flow29</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W562_Flow30</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W562_Task15" name="Review SCO exception log">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 11: Review SCO exception log: access SCO (self-checkout) exception log per W281: (a) review today&#x27;s SCO weight-verification exceptions, (b) review SCO attendant interventions, (c) identify patterns (same customer repeatedly triggering weight exceptions, scan-and-pass behavior), (d) review SCO void rate compared to staffed lanes; flag anomalies for investigation
Responsible (R): Store Manager
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 5–10 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W562_Flow30</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W562_Flow31</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W562_Task16" name="End-of-day LP daily log submission">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 12: End-of-day LP daily log submission: LP Officer completes daily checklist in LP module: (a) all checklist items marked pass/fail/NA with notes, (b) summary of findings (exceptions found, investigations opened, maintenance requests), (c) escalation items for follow-up (Regional LP Officer, Store Manager, HR), (d) overall LP risk assessment for the day (Green/Yellow/Red); submit log; system stores daily log and feeds data into: (a) W37 monthly LP dashboard, (b) W466 quarterly LPAP review, (c) W67 store performance scorecard LP metrics
Responsible (R): LP Officer / Store Manager
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 10 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W562_Flow31</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W562_Flow32</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W562_End17" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W562_Flow32</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W562_Annotation18">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-259 (ensure controlled execution — Store Daily Management (PA-07.1).) | - operational: Store Manager serving as LP proxy with abbreviated daily checklist on non-visit days, and automated W538 exception monitoring filling the gap; operational: yard gate control (W438), customer receipt verification at exit, and CCTV coverage with regular inventory counts; operational: peg hook count reconciliation and gravity bin weight verification
Owner: LP Officer / Store Manager (stores without dedicated LP Officer)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W562_Assoc19" sourceRef="W562_Annotation18" targetRef="W562_Start4" associationDirection="None" />
