        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W702_Task14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W702_Lane6" name="Merchandising Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W702_Task15</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W702_Lane7" name="Marketing">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W702_Task17</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W702_End19</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W702_Start9" name="Board-approved new store location identified; lease signed per W635…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W702_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W702_Task10" name="Project initiation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Project initiation: VP Store Operations appoints Store Opening Project Manager: (a) define project scope: location, target opening date, store format (standard, compact, express), estimated budget; (b) establish project governance: steering committee (VP Store Operations, CFO, CIO), weekly status reporting, milestone review gates; (c) create project plan in PPM tool: 150+ tasks across 10 workstreams with dependencies, durations, and owners; (d) major milestones: lease signed, construction start, construction complete, systems installed, inventory delivered, staff hired and trained, soft launch, grand opening
Responsible (R): Project Manager
Accountable (A): VP Store Operations
Duration: 1 week</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W702_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W702_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W702_Task11" name="Construction &amp; fit-out">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Construction &amp; fit-out: Construction Manager manages build-out per W223: (a) obtain LGU building permits and fire safety permit per W476; (b) construction execution per W224; (c) POS counter, racking, display fixtures, paint mixing station, lumber cutting area installation per W225; (d) final inspection and commissioning per W227; (e) obtain Fire Safety Inspection Certificate (FSIC) from BFP; (f) obtain LGU Certificate of Occupancy; (g) project manager monitors construction milestones and budget
Responsible (R): Construction Manager
Accountable (A): VP Store Operations
Duration: 3-4 months</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W702_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W702_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W702_Task12" name="Utilities &amp; IT infrastructure">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Utilities &amp; IT infrastructure: Facilities Manager and IT coordinate: (a) electricity connection and transformer installation per W701 (3-6 month lead time — initiated during construction); (b) water connection per W701; (c) internet/telecom connection per W701; (d) POS terminals installed and tested (3 terminals per store per model-company profile); (e) network infrastructure: WiFi, CCTV, security alarm system per W71; (f) ERP system configuration: new location created in location master per W508, POS terminal mapping, printer setup, scanner configuration; (g) backoffice computers and handheld devices provisioned
Responsible (R): Facilities Manager / IT Infrastructure Lead
Accountable (A): CIO
Duration: Overlaps with construction</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W702_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W702_Flow25</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W702_Task13" name="Regulatory &amp; compliance setup">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Regulatory &amp; compliance setup: Compliance Officer coordinates: (a) BIR branch registration (apply for BIR Certificate of Registration for new branch — TIN, registered address, books of accounts); (b) LGU business permit for new location; (c) BIR-printed or BIR-registered POS invoices for new branch; (d) DTI price board display compliance; (e) fire safety permit per W476; (f) BFP fire extinguisher inspection; (g) DENR permit if applicable (garden center with water discharge); (h) coordinate with W54 regulatory permits workflow
Responsible (R): Compliance Officer
Accountable (A): VP Legal
Duration: 2-3 months</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W702_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W702_Flow26</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W702_Task14" name="Staffing &amp; training">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Staffing &amp; training: HR Manager coordinates: (a) recruit Store Manager (2-3 months before opening); (b) Store Manager recruits team per the §12.1 roster: 1 ASM, 4 Department Supervisors, 12 Sales Associates, 3 Cashiers, 2 Receiving Clerks, 4 Stock Associates, 1 CSR, 1 Maintenance (~29 FTE per store); (c) all staff complete onboarding per W15 and safety training per W655; (d) cashiers complete POS training per W518; (e) stock associates complete receiving and inventory training per W109; (f) Store Manager and Supervisors complete management training; (g) all certifications current per W655 before opening day
Responsible (R): HR Manager / Store Manager
Accountable (A): CHRO
Duration: 2-3 months before opening</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W702_Flow26</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W702_Flow27</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W702_Task15" name="Merchandising &amp; inventory">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Merchandising &amp; inventory: Merchandising Manager and Supply Chain Manager coordinate: (a) planogram design for new store format per W86; (b) initial assortment selection based on store format and local market per W679; (c) initial stock order placed 4-6 weeks before opening per W2C; (d) initial inventory received and putaway per W109 (typically over 2-3 days); (e) shelf stocking and display setup per W573; (f) price tags and shelf labels printed and placed per W667; (g) promotional displays for grand opening per W583
Responsible (R): Merchandising Manager / Supply Chain Manager
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 4-6 weeks before opening</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W702_Flow27</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W702_Flow28</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W702_Task16" name="Soft launch &amp; readiness verification">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Soft launch &amp; readiness verification: 1-2 weeks before grand opening: (a) conduct soft launch: open store to employees, friends, and family for 2-3 days; (b) test all systems under load: POS transactions, loyalty enrollment, card payments, ecommerce BOPIS routing; (c) verify inventory accuracy: spot-check 100 SKUs across all departments; (d) verify regulatory compliance: BIR invoice printing, senior citizen/PWD discount per W170, price display per W667; (e) Store Manager conducts final walk-through: cleanliness, signage, safety, merchandising standards; (f) fix any issues identified during soft launch
Responsible (R): Project Manager / Store Manager
Accountable (A): VP Store Operations
Duration: 1-2 weeks</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W702_Flow28</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W702_Flow29</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W702_Task17" name="Grand opening">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 8: Grand opening: (a) Marketing coordinates grand opening event per W142: local advertising, social media, PR, community engagement; (b) VP Store Operations or Regional Manager attends grand opening; (c) Store Manager manages opening day operations with full staffing; (d) first-day performance tracked: sales, transactions, customer count, loyalty signups; (e) IT and Helpdesk on standby for system issues per W48
Responsible (R): Marketing / Store Manager
Accountable (A): VP Store Operations
Duration: 1 day</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W702_Flow29</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W702_Flow30</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W702_Task18" name="Post-opening stabilization">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 9: Post-opening stabilization: 30 days after opening: (a) Project Manager conducts post-opening review: sales vs. plan, customer feedback, operational issues, staffing adequacy; (b) Store Manager receives intensive coaching from Regional Manager during first 90 days; (c) merchandising adjustments based on actual sales mix vs. plan; (d) project close-out: final budget reconciliation, lessons learned documentation, project file archived per W255; (e) handover from Project Manager to Regional Manager for ongoing management
Responsible (R): Project Manager / Regional Manager
Accountable (A): VP Store Operations
Duration: 30 days post-opening</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W702_Flow30</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W702_Flow31</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W702_End19" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W702_Flow31</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W702_Annotation20">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-259 (ensure controlled execution — Store Daily Management (PA-07.1).) | - operational: VP Store Operations (project sponsor); Store Opening Project Manager review and approval gate; operational: periodic reconciliation against source documents
Owner: VP Store Operations (project sponsor); Store Opening Project Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W702_Assoc21" sourceRef="W702_Annotation20" targetRef="W702_Start9" associationDirection="None" />
