    <bpmn:process id="W_W703" name="W703. Store Closure, Consolidation &amp; Asset Recovery" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Board-approved store closure/consolidation decision; lease expiry with non-renewal; sustained underperformance; strategic market exit; force majeure (disaster damage beyond repair)
Frequency: Ad-hoc; estimated 2-5 closures/consolidations per year based on portfolio optimization
Volume: Each closure is a 2-4 month project; store inventory value typically PHP 15-30M per location
Owner: VP Store Operations (project sponsor)
Participants: Real Estate Manager, Store Manager, HR Manager, Finance Controller, CIO, Merchandising Manager, Supply Chain Manager, Legal Counsel, Facilities Manager
Source: workflow W703 — Store Closure, Consolidation &amp; Asset Recovery</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W703_LaneSet9">
        <bpmn:lane id="W703_Lane1" name="VP Store Operations">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W703_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W703_Task19</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W703_Start10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W703_Lane2" name="HR Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W703_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W703_Lane3" name="Merchandising Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W703_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W703_Lane4" name="Facilities Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W703_Task14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W703_Lane5" name="CIO">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W703_Task15</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W703_Lane6" name="Compliance Officer">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W703_Task16</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W703_Lane7" name="Real Estate Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W703_Task17</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W703_Lane8" name="Finance Controller">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W703_Task18</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W703_End20</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W703_Start10" name="Board-approved store closure/consolidation decision; lease expiry with non-renewal…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W703_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W703_Task11" name="Closure decision &amp; announcement">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Closure decision &amp; announcement: (a) Board approves closure with specific rationale: underperformance, lease expiry, strategic consolidation, or force majeure; (b) VP Store Operations appoints Closure Project Manager; (c) Legal reviews lease termination provisions: notice period required (typically 60-90 days), early termination penalties, security deposit recovery, restoration obligations; (d) communicate closure timeline to Store Manager (confidential until public announcement); (e) public announcement: VP Store Operations and Marketing coordinate community and media communication; (f) customer notification per W708: notify loyalty members in store&#x27;s trade area of closure and nearest alternative location
Responsible (R): VP Store Operations / Legal
Accountable (A): CEO
Duration: 1-2 weeks</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W703_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W703_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W703_Task12" name="Employee separation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Employee separation: HR Manager coordinates: (a) DOLE-compliant separation process per Philippine Labor Code: 30-day written notice to affected employees, report to DOLE Regional Office per Article 298 (formerly 283) for closures affecting 50+ employees; (b) separation pay computation: 1 month pay per year of service for closures due to redundancy or retrenchment per W643 final pay framework; (c) offer relocation to nearby BuildRight stores for employees willing to transfer (especially Store Managers and Supervisors); (d) outplacement support: job fair with local employers, reference letters, DOLE employment assistance referral; (e) ensure all final pay, 13th month, unused leave, and tax documents (BIR 2316) are prepared per W643
Responsible (R): HR Manager
Accountable (A): CHRO
Duration: 30-60 days</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W703_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W703_Flow25</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W703_Task13" name="Inventory liquidation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Inventory liquidation: Merchandising Manager coordinates: (a) plan liquidation timeline: 4-6 weeks of clearance sales before final closure; (b) progressive markdown schedule: week 1-2: 20-30% off, week 3-4: 40-50% off, final week: 60-80% off; (c) advertise clearance sale per W142 marketing campaigns; (d) items not sold during clearance: transfer to nearest BuildRight store or DC for redistribution; (e) unsaleable items (damaged, expired): write off per W91/W92; (f) final inventory count: physical count on last operating day for financial reconciliation
Responsible (R): Merchandising Manager / Store Manager
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 4-6 weeks</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W703_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W703_Flow26</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W703_Task14" name="Asset recovery">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Asset recovery: Facilities Manager coordinates: (a) catalog all BuildRight-owned assets: POS terminals, racking, display fixtures, refrigeration units, paint mixing station, lumber cutting equipment, security cameras, IT equipment; (b) assess asset condition and recovery value: reusable (transfer to other locations or new store openings), sellable (sell to used equipment buyers), scrap (dispose per W443); (c) coordinate physical removal and logistics; (d) update fixed asset register per W184 and compute gain/loss on asset disposal; (e) ensure all assets removed before lease handover
Responsible (R): Facilities Manager / Finance
Accountable (A): COO
Duration: 2-4 weeks</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W703_Flow26</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W703_Flow27</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W703_Task15" name="System &amp; IT decommissioning">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: System &amp; IT decommissioning: CIO coordinates: (a) deactivate POS terminals and unregister from BIR per FIN-010; (b) decommission ERP location master per W508 (mark as inactive, not deleted for historical data retention); (c) deactivate user accounts for departing staff; (d) cancel internet/telecom service per W701; (e) retrieve IT equipment (terminals, handhelds, routers, printers); (f) ensure all data backed up per W256 retention policy; (g) wipe all devices of BuildRight data per W647 data privacy requirements
Responsible (R): CIO
Accountable (A): CIO
Duration: 1-2 weeks</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W703_Flow27</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W703_Flow28</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W703_Task16" name="Regulatory closure filings">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Regulatory closure filings: Compliance Officer coordinates: (a) BIR branch closure registration: file closure notice with BIR Revenue District Office, surrender unused BIR-registered invoices, obtain Certificate of Registration cancellation; (b) LGU business permit cancellation; (c) DOLE closure report (if 50+ employees affected); (d) cancel DENR permits if applicable; (e) cancel local insurance policies; (f) notify PhilHealth, Pag-IBIG, SSS of employee separations
Responsible (R): Compliance Officer
Accountable (A): VP Legal
Duration: 1-2 months</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W703_Flow28</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W703_Flow29</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W703_Task17" name="Lease handover">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Lease handover: Real Estate Manager coordinates: (a) restore premises to lease-required condition (remove BuildRight fixtures, repair walls, repaint if required by lease); (b) schedule landlord walk-through inspection; (c) negotiate security deposit return (typically 2-3 months rent); (d) settle any outstanding rent or utility balances; (e) formal lease termination agreement signed by both parties per W688; (f) utility disconnection and final billing per W701
Responsible (R): Real Estate Manager / Legal
Accountable (A): COO
Duration: 2-4 weeks</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W703_Flow29</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W703_Flow30</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W703_Task18" name="Financial close-out">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 8: Financial close-out: Finance Controller: (a) final P&amp;L for closed store: revenue through closure date, all closure costs (employee separation, lease penalties, inventory write-off, asset disposal loss, removal costs); (b) compare closure costs to Board-approved budget; (c) capital gain/loss on leasehold improvements (if any); (d) update intercompany positions if store was in different entity per W442; (e) archive store financial records per W256 retention policy; (f) final closure report to CFO and Board
Responsible (R): Finance Controller
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 2-4 weeks</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W703_Flow30</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W703_Flow31</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W703_Task19" name="Post-closure review">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 9: Post-closure review: VP Store Operations conducts post-closure review: (a) document lessons learned for future closures; (b) assess impact on customers in trade area: are they patronizing alternative BuildRight stores or switching to competitors?; (c) assess employee outcomes: how many transferred vs. separated?; (d) compare actual closure costs vs. budget; (e) update store portfolio strategy if closure was part of broader optimization
Responsible (R): VP Store Operations
Accountable (A): CEO
Duration: 2 weeks post-closure</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W703_Flow31</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W703_Flow32</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W703_End20" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W703_Flow32</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W703_Annotation21">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-259 (ensure controlled execution — Store Daily Management (PA-07.1).) | - operational: VP Store Operations (project sponsor) review and approval gate; operational: periodic reconciliation against source documents
Owner: VP Store Operations (project sponsor)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
