        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W826_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W826_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W826_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W826_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W826_End12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W826_Start4" name="Layaway installment payment due per schedule created in W75; payment overdue &gt; 7 days">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W826_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W826_Task5" name="System generates daily overdue layaway report — categorized by aging bucket…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: System generates daily overdue layaway report — categorized by aging bucket: (a) payment due in next 3 days (pre-due reminder queue), (b) 7 days overdue (first notice queue), (c) 14 days overdue (second notice/final notice queue), (d) 30 days overdue (forfeiture eligible queue); report includes: customer name, contact number, layaway plan number, item description, total plan value, payments made, balance due, overdue installment amount, days overdue
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W826_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W826_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W826_Task6" name="Pre-due reminder">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Pre-due reminder (3 days before payment due): system sends automated reminder to customer via W708 — SMS preferred channel (Philippine mobile penetration ~95%), email backup: (a) payment amount due, (b) due date, (c) payment options — in-store at any BuildRight, GCash per W99, bank transfer to BuildRight account, (d) consequence of missed payment: &quot;If payment is not received by [date], your layaway may be subject to cancellation. Please contact us to discuss payment arrangements.&quot;
Responsible (R): System / CSR
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Automated (&lt; 1 min)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W826_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W826_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W826_Task7" name="First overdue notice">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: First overdue notice (7 days overdue): CSR calls customer using contact number from layaway agreement: (a) confirms customer received pre-due reminder, (b) asks about payment intention — &quot;When can you make your installment payment?&quot;, (c) offers one-time payment extension (max 14 additional days) with Store Manager approval for customers with good payment history (2+ on-time payments), (d) documents call outcome in system: &quot;committed to pay by [date]&quot;, &quot;requested extension&quot;, &quot;unable to reach customer&quot;, &quot;customer requests cancellation&quot;
Responsible (R): CSR
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 5-10 min per call</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W826_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W826_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W826_Task8" name="Final notice">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Final notice (14 days overdue): CSR sends formal notice via W708 — registered SMS or email with read receipt: (a) states current overdue amount and total remaining balance, (b) warns: &quot;This is your final notice. Per BuildRight layaway policy, your layaway plan will be cancelled if full overdue balance is not received within 14 days from this notice date [specific date].&quot;, (c) provides store contact number for payment arrangement, (d) explains forfeiture policy — deposit disposition per customer&#x27;s election at plan creation
Responsible (R): CSR
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 5 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W826_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W826_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W826_Task9" name="Forfeiture processing">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Forfeiture processing (30 days overdue, grace period expired, no response or no payment): (a) Store Manager reviews layaway account — verifies customer contact history (all reminders and notices sent, call outcomes documented), approves forfeiture, (b) system cancels layaway agreement — layaway status changes to &quot;Forfeited&quot;, (c) reserved inventory released back to available stock per POS-020 layaway inventory reservation — items return to sellable on-hand, (d) deposit forfeiture calculation per policy: Option A — full deposit forfeited (Dr. Cash / Cr. Forfeiture Income); Option B — deposit less cancellation fee (PHP 500 or 10% of deposit, whichever is higher) returned as store credit per W28 gift card/store credit issuance, (e) system posts forfeiture accounting entries — forfeiture income recognized, layaway liability cleared, inventory reservation released, (f) customer notified of forfeiture via W708 with deposit disposition explanation and store credit reference number if applicable
Responsible (R): CSR / Store Manager
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 15-20 min per forfeiture</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W826_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W826_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W826_Task10" name="Partial payment layaway forfeiture">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Partial payment layaway forfeiture: if customer made some installments but forfeits: (a) calculate total payments made vs. total plan value, (b) apply forfeiture policy — typically all payments converted to store credit less cancellation fee (PHP 500 or 10% of total payments, whichever is higher), (c) store credit issued per W28 — can be used for any future purchase at any BuildRight store, (d) never refund cash for forfeited layaways per policy (deters strategic layaway abuse — customer using layaway to lock sale price then canceling), (e) accounting: Dr. Layaway Liability / Cr. Store Credit Liability (for credit issued) + Cr. Forfeiture Income (for cancellation fee retained)
Responsible (R): CSR
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 10 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W826_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W826_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W826_Task11" name="Monthly layaway analytics report generated by system: (a) plan creation rate by…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Monthly layaway analytics report generated by system: (a) plan creation rate by store and by category, (b) completion rate — target &gt;85% of plans completed without forfeiture, (c) forfeiture rate by store (flag stores &gt;10% forfeiture for investigation), by category (flag categories &gt;15% forfeiture for policy review), and by customer segment, (d) average plan duration (target: &lt;60 days), (e) deposit forfeiture income — recognized monthly in GL, (f) payment reminder effectiveness — conversion rate from pre-due reminder to payment (target: &gt;70%), first notice to payment (target: &gt;50%), final notice to payment (target: &gt;30%)
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): Store Manager / Finance
Duration: 2 hours/month review</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W826_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W826_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W826_End12" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W826_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W826_Annotation13">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-259 (ensure controlled execution — Store Daily Management (PA-07.1).) | - operational: multi-channel notification (SMS + email + call) and system-logged contact history; operational: flag for repeat cancelers (&gt;2 forfeitures in 12 months); operational: calculation per W826
Owner: CSR</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W826_Assoc14" sourceRef="W826_Annotation13" targetRef="W826_Start4" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W826_Flow15" sourceRef="W826_Start4" targetRef="W826_Task5" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W826_Flow16" sourceRef="W826_Task5" targetRef="W826_Task6" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W826_Flow17" sourceRef="W826_Task6" targetRef="W826_Task7" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W826_Flow18" sourceRef="W826_Task7" targetRef="W826_Task8" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W826_Flow19" sourceRef="W826_Task8" targetRef="W826_Task9" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W826_Flow20" sourceRef="W826_Task9" targetRef="W826_Task10" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W826_Flow21" sourceRef="W826_Task10" targetRef="W826_Task11" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W826_Flow22" sourceRef="W826_Task11" targetRef="W826_End12" />
    </bpmn:process>
