    <bpmn:process id="W_W958" name="W958. Store-Level Daily Cash Variance Threshold Monitoring &amp; Exception Escalation" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: POS end-of-day closing process detects cash variance exceeding predefined thresholds
Frequency: ~200–400 variance events/month chain-wide (1–2 per store/month exceeding threshold)
Volume: 1 POS terminal per event; variance range PHP 50–5,000+
Owner: Store Manager
Participants: Cashier, Store Manager, Loss Prevention Officer, Finance (Cash Office), Regional Manager (high-variance escalation)
Source: workflow W958 — Store-Level Daily Cash Variance Threshold Monitoring &amp; Exception Escalation</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W958_LaneSet5">
        <bpmn:lane id="W958_Lane1" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W958_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W958_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W958_Start6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W958_Lane2" name="Cashier">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W958_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W958_Lane3" name="Store Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W958_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W958_Lane4" name="Finance">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W958_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W958_End12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W958_Start6" name="POS end-of-day closing process detects cash variance exceeding predefined thresholds">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W958_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W958_Task7" name="Automated Variance Detection">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Automated Variance Detection: At POS end-of-day closing per W574: (a) system calculates cash variance per terminal: (system expected cash from Z-read) minus (physical cash count by cashier + Store Manager dual count); (b) system applies variance thresholds: (i) Green: ≤ PHP 50 absolute variance — acceptable, no action; (ii) Yellow: PHP 50.01–200 — acceptable, logged for trending; (iii) Orange: PHP 200.01–1,000 — requires cashier explanation and Store Manager investigation; (iv) Red: &gt; PHP 1,000 — mandatory investigation, LP Officer notification, and Regional Manager alert; (c) system automatically categorizes each terminal&#x27;s variance and sends alerts per threshold level
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W958_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W958_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W958_Task8" name="Cashier Explanation &amp; Store Manager Investigation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Cashier Explanation &amp; Store Manager Investigation: For Orange and Red variances: (a) Cashier completes Variance Explanation Form (digital, in POS system): (i) variance amount (over or short); (ii) possible cause (customer rush, no time to count change, system error, counterfeit bill received, multi-tender confusion, POS malfunction); (b) Store Manager investigates: (i) reviews transaction log for suspicious voids, refunds, or discounts per W538; (ii) checks CCTV at checkout area per W838 for visible incidents; (iii) interviews cashier (brief, non-accusatory per W562 LP protocol); (iv) reviews cashier&#x27;s variance history (rolling 30-day trend per cashier ID); (v) checks if variance coincides with shift handover per W517
Responsible (R): Cashier / Store Manager
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 15–30 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W958_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W958_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W958_Task9" name="Resolution &amp; Documentation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Resolution &amp; Documentation: Store Manager determines cause: (a) identified cause — system error, cashier mistake, counterfeit bill, POS glitch: (i) documents cause and corrective action in variance log; (ii) if cashier error: coaching per W518 POS training; recurring errors → retraining mandate per W522; (iii) if counterfeit: logs per W842 LP protocol, notifies bank per W89; (b) unidentified cause: (i) variance logged as &quot;unexplained&quot;; (ii) LP Officer reviews per W837 exception-based reporting within 48 hours; (iii) if unexplained variance persists for same cashier over 3 occurrences in 30 days → LP investigation per W839 internal theft protocol; (c) all variances posted to GL: overs deposited to store cash over account; shorts charged to Store Manager&#x27;s cash accountability ledger (recoverable per company policy after investigation)
Responsible (R): Store Manager / LP Officer
Accountable (A): Regional Manager
Duration: 10–20 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W958_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W958_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W958_Task10" name="Automated Trending &amp; Predictive Alerting">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Automated Trending &amp; Predictive Alerting: System continuously analyzes: (a) per-cashier variance trend (rolling 30-day); (b) per-store aggregate variance trend (rolling 30-day); (c) per-terminal variance pattern (may indicate hardware issue); (d) system generates predictive alerts: (i) &quot;Cashier X has 3+ Yellow variances in 7 days — trending toward Orange&quot;; (ii) &quot;Store Y aggregate cash variance exceeds 0.05% of monthly cash sales — above chain average&quot;; (iii) &quot;Terminal Z shows consistent small shorts (PHP 10–30) — possible calibration issue&quot;; alerts pushed to Store Manager and LP Officer for proactive intervention
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): LP Manager / Regional Manager
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W958_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W958_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W958_Task11" name="Monthly Cash Variance Reporting">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Monthly Cash Variance Reporting: (a) Finance generates monthly cash variance report per store: total overs, total shorts, net variance, % of cash sales, investigation outcomes; (b) LP reviews chain-wide trending: top 10 stores by variance rate, top 10 cashiers by variance frequency, terminal-specific patterns; (c) quarterly: Finance reviews and adjusts variance thresholds based on actual performance data; (d) annual: Internal Audit includes cash variance monitoring in store audit per W121 operational audit
Responsible (R): Finance / LP Manager / Internal Audit
Accountable (A): CFO / VP Store Operations
Duration: 4–6 hours/month (Finance + LP)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W958_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W958_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W958_End12" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W958_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
