    <bpmn:process id="W_W1051" name="W1051. Store-Level Fire Extinguisher Monthly Inspection, Annual Recharge &amp; BFP Compliance" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Monthly recurring schedule (1st business day of each month); or annual recharge due date; or after any discharge event
Frequency: Monthly inspection: 12/year per store; Annual recharge: 1/year per extinguisher
Volume: 1 inspection round per store per month covering all extinguishers; 200 stores × 15–20 extinguishers per store = ~3,000–4,000 extinguishers chain-wide
Owner: Store Manager
Participants: Maintenance/Utility Staff, Store Manager, BFP-Accredited Fire Safety Service Provider
Source: workflow W1051 — Store-Level Fire Extinguisher Monthly Inspection, Annual Recharge &amp; BFP Compliance</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1051_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1051_Lane1" name="Maintenance">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1051_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1051_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1051_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1051_Lane2" name="Store Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1051_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1051_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1051_End9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1051_Start4" name="Monthly recurring schedule (1st business day of each month); or annual recharge due date…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1051_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1051_Task5" name="Monthly Visual Inspection (Each Extinguisher)">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Monthly Visual Inspection (Each Extinguisher): Maintenance/Utility Staff performs 12-point visual inspection of each fire extinguisher using BFP inspection checklist: (a) extinguisher is in its designated location per store floor plan; (b) access path to extinguisher is unobstructed (minimum 1m clearance); (c) extinguisher signage is visible and legible; (d) pressure gauge needle is in the green zone (for pressurized types); (e) safety pin and tamper seal are intact; (f) hose and nozzle are undamaged and unblocked; (g) extinguisher body has no visible damage, corrosion, or dents; (h) operating instructions on label are legible; (i) maintenance tag is attached and inspection dates are current; (j) extinguisher is within its service life (dry chemical: 5 years from manufacture; CO₂: 10 years); (k) weight is within acceptable range (lift test — if noticeably lighter than labeled weight, may have lost pressure or charge); (l) if any item fails: tag extinguisher as &quot;OUT OF SERVICE,&quot; remove from location, place backup extinguisher (stores maintain 10% spare), and create maintenance work order per W47 for immediate service
Responsible (R): Maintenance/Utility Staff
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 3–5 min per extinguisher × 15–20 extinguishers = 45–100 min per store per month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1051_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1051_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1051_Task6" name="Inspection Documentation &amp; Digital Logging">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Inspection Documentation &amp; Digital Logging: (a) for each extinguisher: Maintenance/Utility Staff scans extinguisher barcode/QR code (linked to asset master per W399), selects pass/fail for each of the 12 inspection points, and takes photo of pressure gauge; (b) system auto-populates: extinguisher ID, location, type (ABC dry chem/CO₂/other), capacity, manufacturer, last service date, next service due date; (c) system stores inspection record with timestamp, inspector name, and photo evidence; (d) if all 12 points pass: system marks extinguisher as &quot;Inspected — Compliant&quot; with next monthly inspection date; (e) if any point fails: system creates maintenance work order (W47) and flags for immediate corrective action; (f) system generates store-level monthly compliance summary: total extinguishers, passed, failed, corrective actions taken; (g) Store Manager reviews and signs off on monthly summary
Responsible (R): Maintenance/Utility Staff / System
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 5–10 min (documentation per store)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1051_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1051_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1051_Task7" name="Annual Professional Servicing &amp; Recharge">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Annual Professional Servicing &amp; Recharge: Once per year (per extinguisher service anniversary date), Store Manager coordinates with BFP-accredited fire safety service provider: (a) service provider performs on-site professional servicing: (i) discharge test (verify extinguisher agent discharge correctly); (ii) internal inspection of cylinder and valve assembly; (iii) hydrostatic pressure test for CO₂ and dry chemical cylinders per BFP schedule; (iv) refill/recharge extinguisher agent to specified weight/pressure; (v) replace safety pin and tamper seal; (vi) attach new BFP-accredited service tag with service date and provider license number; (b) any extinguisher failing hydrostatic test or found to have cylinder damage is condemned and must be replaced — Store Manager initiates capex request per W21 or operating expense per W136 (indirect procurement); (c) service provider issues BFP-compliant service certificate for the store; (d) system updates fire extinguisher asset records per W399 with new service date, next service due, and service provider details; (e) service certificate uploaded to compliance document repository per W255 (electronic document storage)
Responsible (R): Store Manager / BFP-Accredited Service Provider
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 2–4 hours per store per year</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1051_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1051_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1051_Task8" name="BFP Inspection Readiness &amp; Audit Trail">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: BFP Inspection Readiness &amp; Audit Trail: (a) system maintains perpetual compliance dashboard per store: each extinguisher&#x27;s inspection history, service history, and compliance status; (b) if BFP conducts unannounced fire safety inspection per W476 (BFP FSIC management): Store Manager presents: (i) current month&#x27;s inspection records; (ii) annual service certificates for all extinguishers; (iii) extinguisher location floor plan; (iv) maintenance and corrective action records; (c) system generates BFP inspection readiness report on demand; (d) any compliance gaps (missed monthly inspections, overdue annual service) are flagged in the compliance dashboard per W506 (unified regulatory compliance calendar) and escalated to Store Manager and Regional Operations Manager
Responsible (R): Store Manager / System
Accountable (A): Regional Operations Manager
Duration: 10–15 min (report generation)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1051_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1051_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1051_End9" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1051_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1051_Annotation10">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-259 (ensure controlled execution — Store Daily Management (PA-07.1).) | - operational: extinguisher service docket with 60/30-day lead reminders; out-of-service units tagged and swapped same-day
Owner: Store Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1051_Assoc11" sourceRef="W1051_Annotation10" targetRef="W1051_Start4" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1051_Flow12" sourceRef="W1051_Start4" targetRef="W1051_Task5" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1051_Flow13" sourceRef="W1051_Task5" targetRef="W1051_Task6" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1051_Flow14" sourceRef="W1051_Task6" targetRef="W1051_Task7" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1051_Flow15" sourceRef="W1051_Task7" targetRef="W1051_Task8" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1051_Flow16" sourceRef="W1051_Task8" targetRef="W1051_End9" />
    </bpmn:process>
    <bpmndi:BPMNDiagram id="W1051_diag">
      <bpmndi:BPMNPlane id="W1051_plane" bpmnElement="W_W1051">
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1051_Lane1_di" bpmnElement="W1051_Lane1" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="80" width="1160" height="170" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
