    <bpmn:process id="W_W1085" name="W1085. Store-Level Appliance Display Model Lifecycle &amp; Periodic Refresh Management" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Scheduled quarterly appliance display rotation, new model introduction by vendor, display model reaching maximum display age threshold (typically 90–120 days), or vendor-initiated display refresh program
Frequency: Quarterly rotation + ad-hoc vendor refreshes (~4–6 refresh cycles per year per store)
Volume: 15–25 appliance display units per store per rotation cycle (appliances are 5% of SKUs, ~1,750 items, with ~20–30 units on active display per store at any time)
Owner: Department Supervisor (Appliances Section)
Participants: Sales Associate (Appliance Section), Receiving Clerk, Store Manager, Merchandising Category Manager (HQ)
Source: workflow W1085 — Store-Level Appliance Display Model Lifecycle &amp; Periodic Refresh Management</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1085_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1085_Lane1" name="Department Supervisor">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1085_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1085_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1085_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1085_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1085_Lane2" name="Category Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1085_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1085_Lane3" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1085_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1085_End11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1085_Start5" name="Scheduled quarterly appliance display rotation, new model introduction by vendor, display…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1085_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1085_Task6" name="Display Age &amp; Condition Assessment">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Display Age &amp; Condition Assessment: (a) system generates quarterly display aging report for each store: listing all appliance display units by SKU, date placed on display, days on display, and original cost; (b) Department Supervisor physically inspects each display unit: cosmetic condition (scratches, dents, discoloration), functional condition (powered on, all features working, remote control present), cleanliness, shelf label accuracy (correct model number, price, specifications), and visual merchandising compliance (per planogram per W314); (c) Supervisor rates each unit: Grade A (like-new, suitable for continued display), Grade B (minor cosmetic wear, can continue display with discount note), Grade C (significant wear, functional but visually impaired, candidate for immediate retirement); (d) assessment results entered into ERP against each display unit&#x27;s serial number
Responsible (R): Department Supervisor
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 2–3 hrs per assessment (quarterly)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1085_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1085_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1085_Task7" name="Rotation Decision &amp; Vendor Coordination">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Rotation Decision &amp; Vendor Coordination: (a) for units exceeding 90-day display age: system flags for rotation review; (b) Category Manager (HQ) reviews flags and determines rotation plan: (i) extend display period for strong-selling models with Grade A condition; (ii) initiate vendor-funded display refresh for models where vendor has co-op display program per W513; (iii) retire and sell display unit as demo model per W524; (iv) transfer to another store in the region where the model is not yet on display per W22 (stock transfers); (c) for vendor-funded refresh: Category Manager contacts vendor for new display unit shipment and return/replacement of old unit; (d) new model introduction: when a vendor launches a new appliance model, Category Manager schedules phased rollout across stores (not all 200 stores receive simultaneously; priority by region and store tier); (e) rotation schedule communicated to each affected store via ERP task notification
Responsible (R): Category Manager (HQ)
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 4–6 hrs per quarterly cycle</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1085_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1085_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1085_Task8" name="Display Unit Retirement &amp; Demo Sale Preparation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Display Unit Retirement &amp; Demo Sale Preparation: For units designated for retirement: (a) Department Supervisor powers down, disconnects, and cleans unit; (b) Receiving Clerk performs condition report: documents all cosmetic defects with photos, confirms all accessories present (remote, manual, mounting hardware, warranty card), and verifies functional test; (c) system reclassifies inventory from &quot;Display Asset&quot; to &quot;Demo/Open-Box Saleable&quot; per W549 (damaged &amp; open-box discount processing); (d) system calculates demo sale price: original SRP × discount factor based on condition grade (Grade A: 10–15% off SRP, Grade B: 20–30% off SRP, Grade C: 35–50% off SRP); (e) demo price approved by Store Manager for Grade A/B discounts; Grade C discounts require Category Manager approval via ERP workflow; (f) unit placed on demo sale display area with prominent &quot;Display Model Sale&quot; signage, condition disclosure, and modified warranty terms (typically: 6-month store warranty instead of manufacturer&#x27;s full warranty)
Responsible (R): Department Supervisor / Receiving Clerk
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 30–45 min per unit</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1085_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1085_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1085_Task9" name="New Display Unit Receipt &amp; Setup">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: New Display Unit Receipt &amp; Setup: (a) Receiving Clerk receives new display unit from vendor or DC transfer; (b) unboxes and performs initial inspection for shipping damage; (c) Department Supervisor sets up unit on display floor: mounts/positions per planogram (W314), connects to power (ensuring proper electrical load per W985 if air conditioner), programs demo mode (continuous operation mode for display), attaches price tag and feature callout cards, updates shelf label in ERP per W181; (d) system updates display tracking record: new SKU, serial number, date placed on display, expected rotation date (90 days), display location (aisle, bay, shelf position); (e) for air conditioners: Store Manager ensures dedicated electrical circuit for display to avoid tripping store breakers; (f) old display unit&#x27;s serial number is deactivated from display tracking and activated in demo sale inventory
Responsible (R): Department Supervisor / Receiving Clerk
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 45–60 min per unit</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1085_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1085_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1085_Task10" name="Display Inventory Reconciliation &amp; Financial Reporting">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Display Inventory Reconciliation &amp; Financial Reporting: (a) monthly: system generates display inventory valuation report per store showing total capital locked in display models, aging profile, and demo sale revenue; (b) quarterly: Category Manager reviews display ROI — sales generated per display unit vs. capital employed; (c) vendor co-op display funding reconciliation: system matches vendor display invoices against co-op advertising budget per W513; (d) demo sale revenue tracked separately in P&amp;L per store; (e) inventory accuracy: display units included in cycle count per W6 (cycle counting) — verified by serial number during monthly count
Responsible (R): System / Category Manager
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: Monthly report: 30 min; Quarterly review: 2–3 hrs</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1085_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1085_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1085_End11" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1085_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1085_Annotation12">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-259 (ensure controlled execution — Store Daily Management (PA-07.1).) | - operational: per W62 (vendor contract lifecycle)
Owner: Department Supervisor (Appliances Section)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1085_Assoc13" sourceRef="W1085_Annotation12" targetRef="W1085_Start5" associationDirection="None" />
