    <bpmn:process id="W_W1091" name="W1091. Store-Level Customer Fence &amp; Gate Installation Service Partner Coordination" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Customer purchases fencing materials (GI sheets, hollow blocks, steel bars, chain-link fence, gate hardware) and requests installation service, or Sales Associate proactively offers installation coordination during fence material estimation per W987
Frequency: ~2,500–4,000 coordination requests/month across all stores (fencing is a common project for Filipino homeowners securing their property perimeter)
Volume: 1 fence/gate installation project coordination per request
Owner: Trade Counter / Pro Desk Supervisor
Participants: Sales Associate (Trade Counter / Lumber &amp; Building Materials), Installation Service Partner (accredited fence contractor), Customer
Source: workflow W1091 — Store-Level Customer Fence &amp; Gate Installation Service Partner Coordination</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1091_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1091_Lane1" name="Sales Associate">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1091_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1091_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1091_Lane2" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1091_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1091_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1091_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1091_Lane3" name="Installation Partner">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1091_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1091_End11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1091_Start5" name="Customer purchases fencing materials (GI sheets, hollow blocks, steel bars, chain-link…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1091_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1091_Task6" name="Project Scope &amp; Site Assessment">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Project Scope &amp; Site Assessment: (a) Sales Associate reviews the fence/gate project details from W987 material estimation: fence type (GI sheet, CHB wall, chain-link, steel panel), total fence length (meters), fence height, number and type of gates (swing or sliding, pedestrian or vehicle), and soil condition (clay, sandy, rocky — affects post foundation depth); (b) Associate confirms customer&#x27;s installation service interest and gathers: site address, site accessibility (narrow alley access may limit equipment), power availability for welding (or generator requirement), and target completion timeline; (c) for complex projects (perimeter &gt; 50m, or includes vehicle sliding gate): Associate recommends an on-site visit by the installation partner before quotation
Responsible (R): Sales Associate
Accountable (A): Trade Counter Supervisor
Duration: 5–8 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1091_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1091_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1091_Task7" name="Installation Partner Selection &amp; Quotation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Installation Partner Selection &amp; Quotation: (a) system queries accredited fence/gate installation partners in the customer&#x27;s area per W600 (service contractor accreditation); (b) system displays available partners with: partner name, accreditation level, completed projects count, LGU business permit status, customer rating, service area coverage, and current availability (lead time to start); (c) system auto-selects top-rated available partner or offers customer a choice of 2–3 options; (d) system generates installation cost estimate based on: fence type × linear meter rate, gate fabrication and installation × unit rate, foundation/concrete work × volume rate, welding labor × hour estimate, and equipment rental (if generator or scaffolding needed); (e) installation estimate ranges: GI sheet fence: PHP 800–1,500/linear meter (labor only); CHB perimeter wall: PHP 1,500–3,000/linear meter (labor + concrete); sliding vehicle gate (3m width): PHP 8,000–20,000 (fabrication + installation); (f) combined estimate: materials (from W987) + installation labor = total project cost
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): Trade Counter Supervisor
Duration: 3–5 min (automated)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1091_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1091_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1091_Task8" name="Partner Assignment &amp; Scheduling">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Partner Assignment &amp; Scheduling: (a) customer approves combined materials + installation estimate; (b) system assigns project to selected installation partner and sends notification with: project scope, site address, customer contact, material list, scheduled material delivery date, and target installation start date; (c) system schedules material delivery to customer site: fence posts, GI sheets or CHB, cement, sand, steel bars, and gate materials delivered via BuildRight&#x27;s home delivery service per W19 or W668 (store-level home delivery coordination); (d) installation partner confirms schedule within 24 hours; (e) customer receives confirmation via SMS/email with: installation partner name and contact, scheduled start date, estimated completion date, and BuildRight customer service hotline for issues
Responsible (R): System / Trade Counter Supervisor
Accountable (A): Trade Counter Supervisor
Duration: 5–8 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1091_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1091_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1091_Task9" name="Installation Execution &amp; Quality Monitoring">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Installation Execution &amp; Quality Monitoring: (a) installation partner arrives on-site on scheduled date; (b) partner verifies material delivery completeness against the material list; (c) partner executes installation: (i) fence post hole digging and concrete pouring; (ii) steel frame fabrication (welding for GI sheet fence) or CHB wall laying; (iii) fence material attachment (GI sheet screwing, chain-link tensioning, or steel panel bolting); (iv) gate fabrication (if custom), hanging, and hardware installation; (v) clean-up; (d) customer inspects completed work; (e) partner provides installation warranty certificate (typically 1-year workmanship warranty); (f) system sends customer satisfaction survey via SMS; (g) for any issues: customer contacts BuildRight customer service per W41 (complaint resolution); BuildRight coordinates with installation partner for warranty rework per W795 (service customer complaint &amp; warranty claim)
Responsible (R): Installation Partner / Customer
Accountable (A): Trade Counter Supervisor
Duration: Installation: 1–5 days depending on scope; Monitoring: automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1091_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1091_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1091_Task10" name="Partner Settlement &amp; Performance Tracking">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Partner Settlement &amp; Performance Tracking: (a) upon customer acceptance (step 4d), system triggers payment to installation partner: labor cost per estimate minus 10% retention released after 30-day defect-free period; (b) for trade account customers: installation cost added to monthly billing per W8; for B2C customers: payment collected at POS or via payment link before installation begins; (c) BuildRight earns coordination fee: 8–12% of installation labor cost; (d) system updates partner performance record: on-time start rate, on-time completion rate, customer satisfaction score, warranty rework rate, and safety incident count; (e) quarterly: Trade Counter Supervisor reviews partner performance; underperforming partners placed on probation or replaced per W600 accreditation criteria
Responsible (R): System / Trade Counter Supervisor
Accountable (A): Finance Manager
Duration: Per-project settlement: automated; Quarterly review: 2–3 hrs</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1091_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1091_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1091_End11" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1091_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1091_Annotation12">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-259 (ensure controlled execution — Store Daily Management (PA-07.1).) | - operational: must allow for estimate adjustment with customer approval
Owner: Trade Counter / Pro Desk Supervisor</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1091_Assoc13" sourceRef="W1091_Annotation12" targetRef="W1091_Start5" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1091_Flow14" sourceRef="W1091_Start5" targetRef="W1091_Task6" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1091_Flow15" sourceRef="W1091_Task6" targetRef="W1091_Task7" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1091_Flow16" sourceRef="W1091_Task7" targetRef="W1091_Task8" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1091_Flow17" sourceRef="W1091_Task8" targetRef="W1091_Task9" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1091_Flow18" sourceRef="W1091_Task9" targetRef="W1091_Task10" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1091_Flow19" sourceRef="W1091_Task10" targetRef="W1091_End11" />
    </bpmn:process>
