    <bpmn:process id="W_W1106" name="W1106. Store-Level Community Building Materials Donation &amp; LGU Partnership" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: LGU (barangay/municipality/city) formal donation request, community disaster relief event (W428), annual CSR budget allocation, or corporate social responsibility initiative activation
Frequency: ~2–5 donation requests per store per month; ~400–1,000 total/month across chain
Volume: 1 donation request per event
Owner: Store Manager
Participants: Store Manager, Department Supervisor (Lumber/Building Materials), CMO (Marketing/CSR), VP Legal &amp; Compliance, Receiving Clerk
Source: workflow W1106 — Store-Level Community Building Materials Donation &amp; LGU Partnership</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1106_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1106_Lane1" name="Store Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1106_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1106_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1106_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1106_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1106_Lane2" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1106_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1106_Lane3" name="Stock Associate">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1106_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1106_End11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1106_Start5" name="LGU (barangay/municipality/city) formal donation request, community disaster relief event…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1106_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1106_Task6" name="Donation Request Receipt &amp; Validation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Donation Request Receipt &amp; Validation: (a) Store Manager receives donation request from LGU/community organization — format may be formal letter (with LGU letterhead and barangay captain signature), email, or in-person request; (b) requestor must provide: requesting organization name, authorized signatory, purpose of donation, specific materials and quantities requested, target completion date, and benefit to community; (c) Store Manager validates: (i) request is from a legitimate organization (LGU, registered NGO, public school, religious institution with SEC registration); (ii) request is within BuildRight&#x27;s CSR focus areas (community infrastructure, education, disaster relief, environmental sustainability); (iii) request does not involve political campaign materials or partisan activities; (iv) requesting entity has not received a donation from the same store in the past 6 months (to prevent repeated requests from the same barangay)
Responsible (R): Store Manager
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 15–30 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1106_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1106_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1106_Task7" name="Donation Value Assessment &amp; Approval Routing">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Donation Value Assessment &amp; Approval Routing: (a) Store Manager assesses donation value at SRP (standard retail price): (i) &lt; PHP 5,000: Store Manager approval authority; items from SLOB/clearance inventory preferred (W220); (ii) PHP 5,001–25,000: Regional Manager approval required; (iii) PHP 25,001–100,000: VP Legal &amp; CMO approval required; (iv) &gt; PHP 100,000: CEO/CFO approval required via corporate CSR committee; (b) system checks inventory availability at store and nearby stores; (c) preference given to: (i) SLOB/clearance items that would otherwise be written off, (ii) slow-moving seasonal items, (iii) display/demo units; (d) Store Manager prepares donation authorization form in ERP with: requesting entity details, items and quantities, estimated value, justification, and proposed delivery method
Responsible (R): Store Manager
Accountable (A): Approver per threshold
Duration: 20–30 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1106_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1106_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1106_Task8" name="Inventory Deduction &amp; Donation Documentation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Inventory Deduction &amp; Donation Documentation: (a) upon approval, system generates a zero-value sales order (donation order type) with special pricing = PHP 0.00; (b) inventory deducted from store stock at WAC (weighted average cost); (c) system generates: (i) donation delivery receipt (DDR) — itemized list of donated materials with quantities and SRP values; (ii) BIR-compliant donation certificate — for tax deductibility, includes BuildRight&#x27;s TIN, donee&#x27;s TIN, description and fair market value of goods; (iii) acknowledgment receipt — for donee&#x27;s signature upon receipt; (d) cost of donated goods recorded as CSR expense in GL: debit CSR Expense, credit Inventory; (e) for tax purposes: donation expense is deductible up to a certain percentage of taxable income per NIRC (National Internal Revenue Code); Finance tracks cumulative annual donation expense vs. cap
Responsible (R): System / Store Manager
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 15–20 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1106_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1106_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1106_Task9" name="Donation Staging &amp; Handover">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Donation Staging &amp; Handover: (a) Stock Associate picks donated items from inventory and stages at receiving dock; (b) Receiving Clerk loads donated materials onto requestor&#x27;s vehicle or BuildRight delivery truck (if delivery is approved); (c) requestor&#x27;s authorized representative signs acknowledgment receipt and presents valid ID; (d) photos taken of donated materials and handover for CSR documentation and social media (coordinated with Marketing per W135); (e) Store Manager sends handover confirmation to regional office
Responsible (R): Stock Associate / Receiving Clerk
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 20–45 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1106_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1106_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1106_Task10" name="Post-Donation Reporting &amp; Community Impact Tracking">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Post-Donation Reporting &amp; Community Impact Tracking: (a) Store Manager logs donation completion in CSR module with photos and acknowledgment receipt scan; (b) monthly CSR donation report generated per store and consolidated at corporate: total donations by value, by category, by beneficiary type; (c) Marketing team (W135) follows up with beneficiary for community impact story and social media content; (d) annual CSR report (W694) includes donation statistics; (e) LGU relationship management: Store Manager follows up with barangay captain to ensure materials were used as intended and maintains positive relationship for business permit renewal (W54) and community support
Responsible (R): Store Manager / Marketing
Accountable (A): CMO
Duration: 15 min per donation</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1106_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1106_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1106_End11" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1106_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1106_Annotation12">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-259 (ensure controlled execution — Store Daily Management (PA-07.1).) | - operational: must enforce documentation completeness
Owner: Store Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1106_Assoc13" sourceRef="W1106_Annotation12" targetRef="W1106_Start5" associationDirection="None" />
