    <bpmn:process id="W_W1116" name="W1116. Store-Level Customer Complaint Trend Analysis &amp; Systemic Issue Escalation" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Weekly complaint trend review schedule, or threshold breach alert (complaint volume spike)
Frequency: Weekly (trend analysis); real-time (threshold alerts)
Volume: ~10–15 customer complaints per store per month; ~2,000–3,000/month across chain (per W41)
Owner: Store Manager
Participants: Store Manager, Department Supervisors, Customer Service Rep, Category Manager (escalated), Quality Assurance
Source: workflow W1116 — Store-Level Customer Complaint Trend Analysis &amp; Systemic Issue Escalation</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1116_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1116_Lane1" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1116_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1116_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1116_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1116_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1116_Lane2" name="Department Supervisor">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1116_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1116_Lane3" name="Store Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1116_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1116_End11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1116_Start5" name="Weekly complaint trend review schedule, or threshold breach alert (complaint volume spike)">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1116_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1116_Task6" name="Complaint Data Aggregation &amp; Classification">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Complaint Data Aggregation &amp; Classification: (a) system automatically aggregates all complaint records for the past 7 days from all channels: in-store (POS customer service log), call center (ticketing system W258), email, social media, and online reviews; (b) each complaint is classified by: (i) Category: Product Quality, Pricing Error, Stock Availability, Service Quality, Delivery Issue, Returns/Exchange Issue, Staff Behavior, Store Cleanliness, Safety Concern, Other; (ii) Product: SKU, brand, category; (iii) Severity: Low (minor inconvenience), Medium (financial impact ≤ PHP 5,000), High (financial impact &gt; PHP 5,000 or safety concern), Critical (injury, legal threat, media exposure); (iv) Resolution Status: Resolved, Pending, Escalated, Unresolved; (c) system generates weekly complaint dashboard: total complaints by category, top 10 complained-about SKUs, top 10 complained-about issues, complaints per department, complaints per channel, comparison to prior week and rolling 4-week average
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1116_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1116_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1116_Task7" name="Trend Identification &amp; Threshold Breach Detection">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Trend Identification &amp; Threshold Breach Detection: (a) system performs automated trend detection: (i) Week-over-week increase: any complaint category increasing &gt; 25% WoW triggers alert; (ii) SKU-specific spike: any SKU with ≥ 5 complaints in a week (vs. typical 0–1) triggers product quality alert; (iii) Department-specific spike: any department with complaint rate &gt; 2× its rolling average triggers staff/service alert; (iv) Safety complaints: any complaint mentioning &quot;injury,&quot; &quot;fire,&quot; &quot;electric shock,&quot; &quot;chemical burn,&quot; or &quot;structural failure&quot; auto-escalates to Critical severity regardless of volume; (b) Store Manager reviews dashboard and system-identified trends; (c) Store Manager adds qualitative context: (i) were there external factors (typhoon, holiday rush, construction nearby)? (ii) is a new product in its launch period (expected higher complaints)? (iii) were there staffing issues (absences, new hires)?
Responsible (R): System / Store Manager
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 30–45 min/week</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1116_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1116_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1116_Task8" name="Root Cause Investigation &amp; Local Resolution">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Root Cause Investigation &amp; Local Resolution: (a) for store-level root causes, Store Manager assigns Department Supervisor to investigate: (i) Product Quality issues: inspect affected items, check receiving records, photograph defects; (ii) Service Quality issues: review CCTV footage, observe staff interactions, check POS transaction logs; (iii) Stock Availability issues: review replenishment records, check DC fill rates, verify demand forecast accuracy; (iv) Safety Concerns: immediately quarantine affected product per W875 (product recall inventory quarantine), inspect remaining stock, photograph hazards; (b) Department Supervisor proposes corrective action: (i) staff retraining; (ii) process adjustment; (iii) product return to vendor (W88); (iv) store layout or signage change; (v) product quarantine or removal from shelf; (c) Store Manager approves and tracks implementation
Responsible (R): Department Supervisor
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 1–3 hours/week</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1116_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1116_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1116_Task9" name="Systemic Issue Escalation to Corporate">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Systemic Issue Escalation to Corporate: (a) if root cause investigation reveals a systemic issue beyond store-level resolution, Store Manager escalates: (i) Product quality (multi-store): escalate to Category Manager with evidence — photos, complaint data, batch/lot numbers; Category Manager initiates vendor quality CAPA (W110) or product recall assessment (W873); (ii) Process failure (multi-store): escalate to COO with documentation — similar complaints at other stores suggest a systemic process issue requiring corporate policy change; (iii) Safety concern (any): escalate immediately to VP Legal, COO, and Quality Assurance — potential product recall (W873) or legal liability (W285); (iv) IT system issue: escalate to IT helpdesk (W48) — e.g., POS pricing errors causing widespread customer complaints; (b) escalation documented in complaint tracking system with expected resolution timeline and responsible corporate owner
Responsible (R): Store Manager
Accountable (A): COO (for systemic issues)
Duration: 30–60 min per escalation</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1116_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1116_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1116_Task10" name="Monthly Complaint Performance Report &amp; Continuous Improvement">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Monthly Complaint Performance Report &amp; Continuous Improvement: (a) system generates monthly complaint performance scorecard per store: (i) total complaints per 1,000 transactions (benchmark: &lt; 2 complaints per 1,000 transactions); (ii) average resolution time (target: ≤ 24 hours for Low/Medium, ≤ 4 hours for High, ≤ 1 hour for Critical); (iii) complaint-to-compliment ratio; (iv) repeat complaint rate (same customer complaining &gt; 1 time in 30 days); (v) Net Promoter Score (NPS) correlation; (b) scorecard included in monthly store performance review (W67); (c) trends inform: (i) Category Manager assortment decisions (W679 — delist high-complaint items); (ii) HR training needs (W51 — targeted staff training); (iii) Operations improvement initiatives (process redesign); (iv) Vendor negotiations (W44 — complaint data as leverage for vendor improvement)
Responsible (R): System / Store Manager
Accountable (A): COO
Duration: automated + 1 hour/week review</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1116_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1116_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1116_End11" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1116_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1116_Annotation12">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-259 (ensure controlled execution — Store Daily Management (PA-07.1).) | - operational: Store Manager review and approval gate
Owner: Store Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1116_Assoc13" sourceRef="W1116_Annotation12" targetRef="W1116_Start5" associationDirection="None" />
