    <bpmn:process id="W_W1121" name="W1121. Store-Level Intercom &amp; Public Address System Daily Operations" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Daily store opening procedure (W5A); ongoing throughout operating hours for announcements
Frequency: Daily (opening test); 5–15 announcements per store per day
Volume: 200 stores × 5–15 announcements/day = 1,000–3,000 announcements/day chain-wide
Owner: Store Manager
Participants: Store Manager, Assistant Store Manager, Cashiers, Sales Associates, Customer Service Rep
Source: workflow W1121 — Store-Level Intercom &amp; Public Address System Daily Operations</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1121_LaneSet5">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1121_Lane1" name="Assistant Store Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1121_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1121_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1121_Start6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1121_Lane2" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1121_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1121_Lane3" name="Various Staff">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1121_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1121_Lane4" name="Store Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1121_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1121_End12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1121_Start6" name="Daily store opening procedure (W5A); ongoing throughout operating hours for announcements">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1121_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1121_Task7" name="Daily PA System Opening Test">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Daily PA System Opening Test: (a) Assistant Store Manager conducts daily PA system test during opening procedure (W5A): (i) audio test: brief test announcement at each zone (main sales floor, lumber yard, garden center, backroom/receiving) — verify all speakers are functional; (ii) microphone test: test both the main desk microphone and the wireless roaming microphone (for floor-level announcements); (iii) volume check: ensure volume is audible in each zone but not uncomfortably loud (Philippine municipal noise ordinances typically limit commercial PA to ≤ 70 dB at the property boundary); (iv) emergency system test: verify the pre-recorded emergency evacuation message plays correctly (not during customer hours — tested before store opens); (b) any malfunction logged as maintenance work order per W47 (store facility maintenance) and escalated immediately for emergency system failures
Responsible (R): Assistant Store Manager
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 5–10 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1121_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1121_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1121_Task8" name="Scheduled Promotional &amp; Service Announcements">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Scheduled Promotional &amp; Service Announcements: (a) system auto-plays pre-recorded promotional announcements at scheduled intervals: (i) promotional announcements: 3–5 pre-recorded messages per day, rotated every 2 hours (e.g., &quot;Visit our Paint Department for the Dulux Summer Promo — buy 2 gallons, get 1 free!&quot;; &quot;Today only: DeWalt power drill kit at 20% off — Aisle 8&quot;); (ii) service reminders: &quot;Don&#x27;t forget, BuildRight offers free lumber cutting service — ask at the Lumber counter!&quot;; &quot;Need delivery? Ask our Customer Service desk about same-day delivery options!&quot;; (iii) loyalty enrollment: &quot;Not yet a BuildRight Rewards member? Sign up at any checkout counter and earn points on every purchase!&quot;; (b) promotional content updated weekly by Marketing via central content management system — pushed to all 200 stores automatically; (c) Store Manager approves any store-specific announcements (local fiesta promo, community event); (d) volume of scheduled announcements limited to ≤ 1 per 30 minutes to avoid customer fatigue
Responsible (R): System / Store Manager
Accountable (A): Marketing Manager (content); Store Manager (store-specific)
Duration: automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1121_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1121_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1121_Task9" name="Live Operational &amp; Customer Service Announcements">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Live Operational &amp; Customer Service Announcements: (a) store staff make live announcements as needed: (i) Customer pages: &quot;Mr. Juan Dela Cruz, your BOPIS order is ready for pickup at the Customer Service counter&quot;; (ii) Department calls: &quot;Plumbing Department Supervisor, please call extension 201&quot;; (iii) Cleanup alerts: &quot;Housekeeping to Aisle 5 — spill cleanup needed&quot;; (iv) Receiving notifications: &quot;Receiving Clerk, delivery truck at Bay 2&quot;; (v) Security alerts (coded): &quot;Associate [Name] to Section 3&quot; (pre-agreed code for LP observation needed); (b) announcement protocol: (i) staff must use standard opening: &quot;Attention BuildRight shoppers/Attention BuildRight team&quot;; (ii) no slang, jokes, or personal messages; (iii) no customer full names for privacy (use &quot;Customer with order #[XXX]&quot;) unless customer has explicitly consented to PA paging; (iv) emergency announcements override all other audio (background music, promotional recordings)
Responsible (R): Various Staff
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 30 sec–1 min per announcement</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1121_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1121_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1121_Task10" name="Emergency PA Announcement Procedures">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Emergency PA Announcement Procedures: (a) pre-recorded emergency messages activated by Store Manager or Assistant Store Manager: (i) Fire/Evacuation: &quot;Attention — please evacuate the store immediately through the nearest exit. Do not use elevators. Leave your belongings. Proceed to the assembly point at [location].&quot;; (ii) Severe Weather (Typhoon): &quot;Attention shoppers — due to severe weather conditions, please move to the interior of the store away from windows and doors. Follow staff instructions.&quot;; (iii) Lockdown: &quot;Attention — for safety reasons, please remain inside the store. Follow staff instructions. Do not exit until further notice.&quot;; (iv) All Clear: &quot;Attention — the situation has been resolved. Thank you for your cooperation. Please resume normal activities.&quot;; (b) emergency announcements take priority: system mutes all music and promotional audio; (c) backup: battery-powered megaphone stored at customer service desk in case of total power failure (W580)
Responsible (R): Store Manager
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: immediate</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1121_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1121_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1121_Task11" name="Closing Announcements &amp; Daily System Shutdown">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Closing Announcements &amp; Daily System Shutdown: (a) closing sequence: (i) T-15 minutes: &quot;BuildRight Depot will be closing in 15 minutes. Please bring your final selections to the checkout counter. Thank you for shopping with us!&quot;; (ii) T-5 minutes: &quot;Final call — BuildRight Depot closes in 5 minutes. Please proceed to checkout. Thank you and come again!&quot;; (iii) Closing: &quot;BuildRight Depot is now closed. Thank you for shopping with us today. Our store opens tomorrow at [time]. Have a great evening!&quot;; (b) Assistant Store Manager confirms all customers have exited before initiating closing procedures (W574); (c) PA system switched to standby mode (microphones disabled, background music off, emergency system remains active 24/7)
Responsible (R): Assistant Store Manager
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 5 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1121_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1121_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1121_End12" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1121_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1121_Annotation13">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-259 (ensure controlled execution — Store Daily Management (PA-07.1).) | - operational: battery backup and manual megaphone as mandatory backup measures
Owner: Store Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1121_Assoc14" sourceRef="W1121_Annotation13" targetRef="W1121_Start6" associationDirection="None" />
