    <bpmn:process id="W_W1142" name="W1142. Store-Level Customer Waiting Area Comfort &amp; Amenities Daily Management" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Daily store opening procedure (W5A), or customer complaint about waiting conditions
Frequency: Daily (200 stores)
Volume: 1 waiting area per store (typically near customer service counter)
Owner: Customer Service Rep
Participants: Customer Service Rep, Maintenance/Utility Staff
Source: workflow W1142 — Store-Level Customer Waiting Area Comfort &amp; Amenities Daily Management</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1142_LaneSet2">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1142_Lane1" name="Customer Service Rep">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1142_Task4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1142_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1142_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1142_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1142_Start3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1142_End8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1142_Start3" name="Daily store opening procedure (W5A), or customer complaint about waiting conditions">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1142_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1142_Task4" name="Morning Setup &amp; Cleanliness Check">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Morning Setup &amp; Cleanliness Check: (a) during store opening (W5A), CSR checks waiting area: seating — clean, no damage, adequate number of chairs (minimum 6–8); table surfaces — clean, no stains or damage; lighting — all fixtures working; air conditioning/ventilation — comfortable temperature; floor — clean, no debris, no trip hazards; reading materials — current catalogs, flyers, and promotional materials stocked and organized; loyalty enrollment materials — forms and QR codes available; water dispenser — clean, filled, cups stocked; waste bin — empty or not overflowing; (b) any issues reported to Maintenance/Utility staff for immediate resolution per W47
Responsible (R): Customer Service Rep
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 10–15 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1142_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1142_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1142_Task5" name="Marketing Materials &amp; Content Rotation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Marketing Materials &amp; Content Rotation: (a) CSR reviews displayed marketing materials: are current month&#x27;s promotions displayed? are seasonal catalogs available (current season)? are product brochures for high-margin categories stocked (power tools, appliances, fixtures)? is loyalty program enrollment information visible? (b) rotate materials as needed: remove expired promotions, add new product brochures from vendors (W1128), update digital signage content per W504; (c) place BuildRight&#x27;s &quot;How-To&quot; video QR codes (W1136) — customers can scan to watch tutorials while waiting; (d) ensure &quot;Rate Your Experience&quot; QR code is prominently displayed for real-time feedback
Responsible (R): Customer Service Rep
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 5–10 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1142_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1142_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1142_Task6" name="Mid-Day Comfort Check">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Mid-Day Comfort Check: (a) during lunch break lull, CSR performs mid-day check: temperature comfortable? water dispenser still stocked? seating still clean (after morning customers)? waste bin not overflowing? reading materials not depleted? (b) restock as needed; (c) any customer feedback about comfort addressed immediately — if too warm, check AC and report if malfunctioning per W47
Responsible (R): Customer Service Rep
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 5 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1142_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1142_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1142_Task7" name="End-of-Day Reset">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: End-of-Day Reset: (a) during closing procedure (W574), CSR performs waiting area reset: wipe down all seating and table surfaces; restock water and cups; empty waste bin; organize and replenish reading materials; check for personal items left by customers (route to lost &amp; found per W929); (b) report any maintenance needs for next-day resolution (damaged furniture, broken light, AC issue)
Responsible (R): Customer Service Rep / Maintenance
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 10–15 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1142_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1142_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1142_End8" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1142_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1142_Annotation9">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-259 (ensure controlled execution — Store Daily Management (PA-07.1).) | - operational: Customer Service Rep review and approval gate
Owner: Customer Service Rep</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1142_Assoc10" sourceRef="W1142_Annotation9" targetRef="W1142_Start3" associationDirection="None" />
