    <bpmn:process id="W_W1407" name="W1407. Store Seasonal Department Reset, Category Space Reallocation &amp; New Product Introduction Floor Execution" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Seasonal transition calendar from Merchandising team (W13); new product introduction batch from Category Manager; or post-seasonal clearance completion requiring floor reset
Frequency: 6 major seasonal transitions per year (Jan–Feb post-holiday renovation, Mar–Apr summer, May school build-out, Jun–Aug rainy season, Sep–Oct ber-months, Nov–Dec Christmas — per profile §13.2) + 6 bi-monthly catalog promotion resets = ~12 resets per store per year
Volume: ~200 stores × ~12 resets/year = ~2,400 reset events chain-wide (per the Frequency); each reset involves ~50–200 SKUs being moved, added, or removed per store
Owner: Store Manager
Participants: Store Manager, Department Supervisors (4 per store), Sales Associates, Merchandising Coordinator (HQ visual merchandising team)
Source: workflow W1407 — Store Seasonal Department Reset, Category Space Reallocation &amp; New Product Introduction Floor Execution</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1407_LaneSet6">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1407_Lane1" name="Merchandising Coordinator">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1407_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1407_Task17</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1407_Start7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1407_Lane2" name="Store Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1407_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1407_Task16</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1407_Lane3" name="Department Supervisors">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1407_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1407_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1407_Lane4" name="Sales Associates">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1407_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1407_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1407_Task14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1407_Lane5" name="Department Supervisor">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1407_Task15</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1407_End18</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1407_Start7" name="Seasonal transition calendar from Merchandising team (W13); new product introduction…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1407_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1407_Task8" name="Merchandising Coordinator distributes seasonal reset package to Store Manager 2…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Merchandising Coordinator distributes seasonal reset package to Store Manager 2 weeks before execution window: (a) new planograms for each affected department (the 4 supervisor-led departments — Lumber, Plumbing/Electrical, Tiles, Tools/Hardware — with the Paint, Appliances, and Garden selling areas folded into these supervisor groups per profile §12.1), (b) SKUs to be added (new seasonal introductions with shelf location assignments), (c) SKUs to be removed (end-of-season items to be moved to clearance area or backroom), (d) SKUs to remain but with changed shelf position, (e) new shelf labels and price tags, (f) visual merchandising guidelines (display fixtures, signage, seasonal theme elements)
Responsible (R): Merchandising Coordinator
Accountable (A): Category Manager
Duration: 1 day</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1407_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1407_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1407_Task9" name="Store Manager holds 30-minute reset briefing with all 4 Department Supervisors…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Store Manager holds 30-minute reset briefing with all 4 Department Supervisors: reviews planogram changes by department, assigns each Supervisor to their department, identifies cross-department dependencies (e.g., Garden department expanding into space vacated by seasonal clearance), and sets execution timeline (typically 2–3 evenings or 1 full non-trading day)
Responsible (R): Store Manager
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 30 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1407_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1407_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1407_Task10" name="Department Supervisors print planograms and shelf labels from system; verify…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Department Supervisors print planograms and shelf labels from system; verify they have received all new product shipments (from W4 replenishment) needed for the reset; if any new SKUs have not arrived, escalate to Merchandising Coordinator for expedited shipment or inter-store transfer (W22)
Responsible (R): Department Supervisors
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 1 hour</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1407_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1407_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1407_Task11" name="Phase 1 — Clear out-of-season inventory">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Phase 1 — Clear out-of-season inventory: Department Supervisors direct Sales Associates to physically remove SKUs designated for clearance; move clearance items to designated clearance area (endcap or clearance aisle); update system location for moved SKUs; apply clearance pricing per markdown instructions from Merchandising (W532)
Responsible (R): Department Supervisors / Sales Associates
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 2–3 hours/department</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1407_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1407_Flow25</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1407_Task12" name="Phase 2 — Reallocate shelf space">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Phase 2 — Reallocate shelf space: Sales Associates reconfigure shelving, hooks, and display fixtures per new planogram; adjust shelf heights, add or remove shelf dividers, install new display fixtures for seasonal themes; Department Supervisor verifies physical layout matches planogram
Responsible (R): Sales Associates / Department Supervisors
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 2–3 hours/department</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1407_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1407_Flow26</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1407_Task13" name="Phase 3 — Stock new seasonal SKUs">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Phase 3 — Stock new seasonal SKUs: Sales Associates place new seasonal merchandise on newly configured shelves per planogram; scan each item to verify correct SKU at correct location (system validates SKU-to-location match); apply new shelf labels and price tags
Responsible (R): Sales Associates / Department Supervisors
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 2–4 hours/department</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1407_Flow26</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1407_Flow27</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1407_Task14" name="Phase 4 — Visual merchandising">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Phase 4 — Visual merchandising: Sales Associates install seasonal signage, theme decorations, and point-of-purchase (POP) materials per visual merchandising guidelines; set up product demo stations if applicable (e.g., paint color display for summer, waterproofing demo for rainy season)
Responsible (R): Sales Associates
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 1–2 hours/department</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1407_Flow27</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1407_Flow28</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1407_Task15" name="Department Supervisor walks completed department with Store Manager: verifies…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 8: Department Supervisor walks completed department with Store Manager: verifies planogram compliance (W86), checks shelf labels match system prices, confirms all new SKUs are stocked and clearance items removed, assesses visual merchandising execution; Store Manager signs off or requests corrections
Responsible (R): Department Supervisor / Store Manager
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 30 min/department</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1407_Flow28</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1407_Flow29</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1407_Task16" name="Store Manager photographs completed department reset (before/after photos)…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 9: Store Manager photographs completed department reset (before/after photos); uploads photos to reset completion portal for Merchandising Coordinator review; marks reset as complete in system with date/time stamp
Responsible (R): Store Manager
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 15 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1407_Flow29</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1407_Flow30</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1407_Task17" name="Merchandising Coordinator reviews before/after photos from all 200 stores…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 10: Merchandising Coordinator reviews before/after photos from all 200 stores within 3 business days; flags stores with non-compliant resets for Store Manager follow-up; generates chain-wide reset compliance scorecard for VP Merchandising
Responsible (R): Merchandising Coordinator
Accountable (A): Category Manager
Duration: 4 hours/batch</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1407_Flow30</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1407_Flow31</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1407_End18" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1407_Flow31</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1407_Annotation19">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-259 (ensure controlled execution — Store Daily Management (PA-07.1).) | - operational: Store Manager review and approval gate
Owner: Store Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1407_Assoc20" sourceRef="W1407_Annotation19" targetRef="W1407_Start7" associationDirection="None" />
