    <bpmn:process id="W_W1281" name="W1281. Lumber Yard Daily Operations &amp; Inventory Management" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Daily store opening; lumber yard area walkthrough
Frequency: Daily operations; weekly inventory reconciliation
Volume: ~4,900 lumber &amp; building material SKUs chain-wide (profile §6.2 category count; per-store lumber assortment is a subset); ~200–400 lumber transactions per store per month
Owner: Department Supervisor (Lumber &amp; Building Materials)
Participants: Department Supervisor, Stock Associate, Sales Associate, Receiving Clerk
Source: workflow W1281 — Lumber Yard Daily Operations &amp; Inventory Management</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1281_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1281_Lane1" name="Department Supervisor">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1281_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1281_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1281_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1281_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1281_Lane2" name="Stock Associate">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1281_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1281_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1281_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1281_Lane3" name="Sales Associate">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1281_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1281_End13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1281_Start5" name="Daily store opening; lumber yard area walkthrough">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1281_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1281_Task6" name="Morning yard inspection">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Morning yard inspection: Department Supervisor conducts daily lumber yard walkthrough: (a) check overnight weather impact (rain exposure, standing water), (b) inspect lumber stacks for shifting, leaning, or collapse, (c) verify grade segregation (common, standard, select) is maintained, (d) check rebar and steel racks for rust or misplacement, (e) verify price signs and board foot measurement guides are visible and accurate
Responsible (R): Department Supervisor
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 20 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1281_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1281_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1281_Task7" name="Moisture monitoring">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Moisture monitoring: Stock Associate checks moisture content of sample boards using moisture meter: (a) test 5–10 boards per species (tanguile, apitong, yakal) at top, middle, and bottom of stacks, (b) record readings in mobile app; if moisture &gt;20%: trigger additional protective covering, increase ventilation, or move vulnerable stock under cover per W1275; system logs moisture readings for trend analysis
Responsible (R): Stock Associate
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 15 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1281_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1281_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1281_Task8" name="Stack restacking &amp; organization">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Stack restacking &amp; organization: Stock Associate reorganizes lumber stacks disturbed by previous day&#x27;s sales: (a) restack boards shifted during customer selection, (b) ensure boards are sorted by dimension (2×2, 2×3, 2×4, 2×6) and length (8ft, 10ft, 12ft), (c) move any boards with visible defects (warp, split, rot) to defect staging area for RTV per W1280 or markdown per W93, (d) ensure stack height limits (max 6 feet) are maintained for safety
Responsible (R): Stock Associate
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 30 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1281_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1281_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1281_Task9" name="Catch-weight inventory reconciliation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Catch-weight inventory reconciliation: Weekly, Department Supervisor conducts lumber yard physical count: (a) count board pieces by species, dimension, and length, (b) system compares physical count to book inventory (adjusted for catch-weight sales per W463), (c) investigate variances &gt;5%; common causes: measurement rounding at POS, undocumented customer cutting waste, pilferage of small pieces; (d) post adjustment with approval per threshold
Responsible (R): Department Supervisor
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 2 hours/week</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1281_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1281_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1281_Task10" name="Customer cut-to-length service">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Customer cut-to-length service: Sales Associate operates lumber cutting station for customer requests: (a) measure and mark cut length per customer specification, (b) perform cross-cut using miter saw or circular saw (safety protocol: goggles, push stick, blade guard), (c) weigh or measure resulting pieces for pricing per W463, (d) generate cut-to-length tag with price for POS scanning, (e) log cutting waste (offcuts) for inventory deduction per system configuration
Responsible (R): Sales Associate
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 10 min/cut</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1281_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1281_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1281_Task11" name="Seasonal rotation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Seasonal rotation: Department Supervisor manages seasonal lumber yard transitions: (a) pre-typhoon: reduce outdoor inventory levels, move premium species under cover, secure loose items per W576, (b) post-typhoon: inspect for water damage, re-grade affected lumber, process damaged stock per W1280, (c) summer construction peak: increase safety stock levels per W2A, ensure adequate stacking space
Responsible (R): Department Supervisor
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: Per seasonal event</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1281_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1281_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1281_Task12" name="Daily yard close">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Daily yard close: Stock Associate conducts end-of-day yard close: (a) cover exposed lumber stacks with tarps (overnight rain protection), (b) secure cutting station (unplug tools, store blades), (c) verify all customers have exited yard area, (d) report any inventory discrepancies to Department Supervisor, (e) report any safety hazards (protruding nails, unstable stacks) per W440
Responsible (R): Stock Associate
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 15 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1281_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1281_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1281_End13" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1281_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1281_Annotation14">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-259 (ensure controlled execution — Store Daily Management (PA-07.1).) | - operational: Department Supervisor (Lumber &amp; Building Materials) review and approval gate; operational: periodic reconciliation against source documents
Owner: Department Supervisor (Lumber &amp; Building Materials)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
