    <bpmn:process id="W_W1282" name="W1282. Paint Mixing Station Daily Setup, Color Formula Management &amp; Consumables Replenishment" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Daily store opening for paint mixing station; or consumable stock level triggers reorder
Frequency: Daily setup and close; weekly formula review; bi-weekly consumable replenishment
Volume: ~80–120 paint mixing transactions per store per month; ~2,800 SKU color formula database
Owner: Department Supervisor (Paint &amp; Finishes)
Participants: Sales Associate (Paint), Department Supervisor, Vendor Technical Representative
Source: workflow W1282 — Paint Mixing Station Daily Setup, Color Formula Management &amp; Consumables Replenishment</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1282_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1282_Lane1" name="Sales Associate">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1282_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1282_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1282_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1282_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1282_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1282_Lane2" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1282_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1282_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1282_Lane3" name="Department Supervisor">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1282_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1282_End13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1282_Start5" name="Daily store opening for paint mixing station; or consumable stock level triggers reorder">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1282_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1282_Task6" name="Morning station setup">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Morning station setup: Sales Associate opens paint mixing station: (a) power on tinting machine and shaker, (b) run diagnostic self-test, (c) verify colorant canister levels (12–16 standard colorants: white, black, red, yellow, blue, ochre, etc.) — flag any canister below 20% for priority replenishment, (d) verify base paint inventory within arm&#x27;s reach (flat, semi-gloss, gloss in white and neutral bases), (e) check mixing supplies: stir sticks, can openers, sample cards, mixing cups, drop cloths
Responsible (R): Sales Associate
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 15 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1282_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1282_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1282_Task7" name="Color formula database sync">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Color formula database sync: System automatically syncs color formula updates from paint vendor: (a) new color additions, (b) revised formulas for existing colors (vendor may adjust tint ratios for consistency), (c) seasonal promotional colors (e.g., &quot;BuildRight Summer Collection&quot;), (d) Sales Associate reviews new formulas on tablet and notes any additions for customer communication
Responsible (R): System / Sales Associate
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 5 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1282_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1282_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1282_Task8" name="Custom color matching service">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Custom color matching service: For customers bringing physical samples (paint chip, fabric, tile): (a) Sales Associate scans sample with spectrophotometer per W981, (b) system generates closest formula match with delta-E deviation score, (c) if customer approves: mix test sample (100 ml), customer verifies under store lighting, (d) upon approval: mix full quantity in selected base and sheen, (e) generate custom color label with formula code for reordering, (f) store custom formula in customer&#x27;s loyalty profile for future matching
Responsible (R): Sales Associate
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 15–20 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1282_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1282_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1282_Task9" name="Standard color mixing">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Standard color mixing: For catalog colors: (a) customer selects color from physical fan deck or digital display, (b) Sales Associate enters color code and desired quantity + base type, (c) tinting machine dispenses precise colorant amounts into base can, (d) place can in mechanical shaker for 3–5 minutes, (e) open can for customer color verification, (f) apply color label with batch code and mixing date
Responsible (R): Sales Associate
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 10 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1282_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1282_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1282_Task10" name="Consumable inventory monitoring">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Consumable inventory monitoring: System tracks paint mixing consumable usage: (a) colorant canister levels (auto-detected by tinting machine), (b) base paint inventory (scan-based tracking), (c) mixing cans and lids, (d) sample cards and fan decks; when any item falls below reorder point: system generates replenishment order (a) colorants and base paint from vendor via standard PO per W2A, (b) supplies from DC replenishment per W4
Responsible (R): System / Department Supervisor
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: Automated + 15 min/week review</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1282_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1282_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1282_Task11" name="End-of-day station close">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: End-of-day station close: Sales Associate closes paint mixing station: (a) clean tinting machine nozzles and spillage per manufacturer protocol, (b) wipe down mixing table and shaker, (c) cap all colorant canisters tightly (colorant dries and clogs if exposed overnight), (d) record any equipment issues in maintenance log, (e) secure paint inventory (high-value target for theft per W405), (f) run end-of-day colorant usage report for inventory reconciliation
Responsible (R): Sales Associate
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 15 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1282_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1282_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1282_Task12" name="Weekly formula accuracy review">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Weekly formula accuracy review: Department Supervisor reviews weekly mixing accuracy metrics: (a) customer remix rate (customer rejects first mix and requests adjustment — target &lt;3%), (b) custom color re-match rate (customer returns for same custom color — formula must produce consistent results), (c) colorant consumption variance (actual vs. system-calculated usage — detects machine calibration drift or shrinkage), (d) escalate to vendor technical representative if remix rate &gt;5% or colorant variance &gt;10%
Responsible (R): Department Supervisor
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 30 min/week</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1282_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1282_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1282_End13" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1282_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1282_Annotation14">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-259 (ensure controlled execution — Store Daily Management (PA-07.1).) | - operational: Department Supervisor (Paint &amp; Finishes) review and approval gate; operational: periodic reconciliation against source documents
Owner: Department Supervisor (Paint &amp; Finishes)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
