    <bpmn:process id="W_W1485" name="W1485. Store Paint Mixing Station Daily Calibration, Color Formula Database Update &amp; Tint Inventory Replenishment" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Start of each store operating day; also triggered when new color formula batch is received from HQ Merchandising or tint cartridge stock falls below reorder point
Frequency: Daily calibration; weekly formula update; replenishment as needed
Volume: 1 calibration per store per day (200/day chain-wide); ~4–6 formula updates/month; ~2–3 tint replenishment orders/store/month
Owner: Department Supervisor (Paint &amp; Decor)
Participants: Paint Desk Associate, Department Supervisor, Merchandise Planner (HQ)
Source: workflow W1485 — Store Paint Mixing Station Daily Calibration, Color Formula Database Update &amp; Tint Inventory Replenishment</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1485_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1485_Lane1" name="Paint Desk Associate">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1485_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1485_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1485_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1485_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1485_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1485_Lane2" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1485_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1485_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1485_End11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1485_Start4" name="Start of each store operating day; also triggered when new color formula batch is…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1485_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1485_Task5" name="Daily colorant dispenser calibration">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Daily colorant dispenser calibration: At store opening: (a) Paint Desk Associate runs automated calibration cycle on the tint dispenser; (b) system dispenses measured drops of each of the 12–16 colorants into a calibration vial; (c) vial weight compared to expected weight per colorant; (d) variance &gt; 2% triggers recalibration or cartridge replacement; (e) calibration results logged in system with date, time, and associate ID; (f) if calibration fails after 2 attempts: station flagged as &quot;Calibration Required — Manual Override&quot; and Department Supervisor notified
Responsible (R): Paint Desk Associate
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 10 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1485_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1485_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1485_Task6" name="Tint cartridge inventory check">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Tint cartridge inventory check: After calibration: (a) system reads current fill levels of all tint cartridges from dispenser sensors; (b) cartridges below 20% capacity flagged for reorder; (c) Paint Desk Associate visually confirms cartridge levels for accuracy; (d) replenishment order auto-generated per min/max rules; (e) critical colorants (white, black, red oxide, yellow oxide) that reach &lt; 10% trigger urgent reorder with next-day delivery priority
Responsible (R): Paint Desk Associate / System
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 5 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1485_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1485_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1485_Task7" name="Color formula database sync">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Color formula database sync: When HQ Merchandising releases updated formulas: (a) system downloads new formula batch to store paint mixing terminal; (b) formulas include new supplier color collections, seasonal specials, and corrected formulas from quality feedback; (c) Paint Desk Associate verifies download completion and confirms formula count matches HQ notification; (d) old formulas archived but remain accessible for 90 days for warranty re-matches; (e) test mix of one random new formula to verify output accuracy
Responsible (R): System / Paint Desk Associate
Accountable (A): Merchandise Planner
Duration: 5 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1485_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1485_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1485_Task8" name="Customer color match verification">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Customer color match verification: When a customer brings a physical sample (chip, swatch, object): (a) Paint Desk Associate uses the spectrophotometer to scan the sample; (b) system matches to nearest formula in the database; (c) associate mixes a 50 ml test sample; (d) test sample compared to customer&#x27;s sample under the station&#x27;s daylight-balanced light; (e) if acceptable: full gallon mixed per formula; (f) if not acceptable: associate manually adjusts formula by eye/experience, re-tests; (g) final formula saved as custom mix in customer&#x27;s profile for future reorder
Responsible (R): Paint Desk Associate
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 8–15 min per match</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1485_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1485_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1485_Task9" name="End-of-day tint usage reconciliation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: End-of-day tint usage reconciliation: At store closing: (a) system generates daily tint usage report showing volume dispensed per colorant; (b) actual cartridge level readings vs. calculated usage compared; (c) variance &gt; 5% flagged for investigation (possible leak, evaporation, or dispenser malfunction); (d) daily paint revenue vs. gallons mixed cross-checked for average selling price monitoring
Responsible (R): System / Paint Desk Associate
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 5 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1485_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1485_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1485_Task10" name="Weekly paint station deep clean &amp; maintenance">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Weekly paint station deep clean &amp; maintenance: Weekly: (a) Paint Desk Associate performs deep cleaning of tint dispenser nozzles, mixing area, and spectrophotometer lens; (b) expired or contaminated base paint inventory pulled per PA-05.3 disposition rules; (c) fan deck displays cleaned and damaged/missing cards replaced; (d) any dispenser maintenance issues reported per PA-20.3 equipment maintenance workflow
Responsible (R): Paint Desk Associate
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 30 min/week</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1485_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1485_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1485_End11" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1485_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1485_Annotation12">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-259 (ensure controlled execution — Store Daily Management (PA-07.1).) | - operational: periodic reconciliation against source documents
Owner: Department Supervisor (Paint &amp; Decor)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
