        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1490_Start5" name="Quarterly display refresh cycle; also triggered when display model is damaged, vendor…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1490_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1490_Task6" name="Display model inventory tagging">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Display model inventory tagging: Each display unit: (a) tagged with a &quot;Display Model — Not for Sale&quot; label and unique display asset number; (b) entered in system as display inventory (separate from sellable stock) with: original cost, vendor-provided flag (free/discounted/purchased), installation date, and expected rotation date; (c) linked to the corresponding sellable SKU so customers can scan QR code on display to see pricing and stock availability; (d) display assets tracked separately from regular inventory for cost accounting
Responsible (R): Visual Merchandising Associate
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 10 min per unit</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1490_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1490_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1490_Task7" name="Quarterly display rotation assessment">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Quarterly display rotation assessment: Quarterly: (a) Department Supervisor reviews all display units: physical condition, model currency (is it still in the active catalog?), vendor display allowance status, customer engagement (measured by QR scans per display); (b) units rated as: (i) &quot;Keep&quot; — good condition, current model, high engagement; (ii) &quot;Rotate&quot; — worn or outdated, replace with new model; (iii) &quot;Sell&quot; — good condition but model being discontinued, offer at 20–30% discount to clearance customers; (iv) &quot;Write-off&quot; — damaged, missing parts, unsellable; (c) rotation plan submitted to Merchandise Planner for new model allocation
Responsible (R): Department Supervisor
Accountable (A): Merchandise Planner
Duration: 2–3 hours/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1490_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1490_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1490_Task8" name="Display unit write-off processing">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Display unit write-off processing: For units marked &quot;Write-off&quot;: (a) Department Supervisor initiates write-off request in system with photos of condition and reason code (customer damage, normal wear, vendor defect, weather damage); (b) write-off value = original cost less any vendor display allowance already received; (c) LP Associate performs spot verification for write-offs &gt; PHP 5,000 to rule out theft; (d) Department Supervisor approves write-offs &lt; PHP 10,000; Store Manager approves PHP 10,000–50,000; VP Merchandising approves &gt; PHP 50,000; (e) write-off posted to display expense account (not COGS); (f) physical unit disposed of or returned to vendor for credit per vendor agreement
Responsible (R): Department Supervisor / LP Associate
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 15–30 min per write-off</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1490_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1490_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1490_Task9" name="Customer purchase of display unit">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Customer purchase of display unit: When customer wants to buy the display model: (a) Sales Associate checks if model is still in active catalog and sellable stock is available; (b) if stock available: encourage customer to buy new-in-box at regular price; (c) if stock unavailable or customer insists on display: apply display unit discount (typically 20–40% off); (d) display unit removed from display asset register and sold as a regular transaction with &quot;Display Unit — Sold As-Is&quot; notation; (e) replacement display unit ordered from next replenishment cycle; (f) gap on display wall covered with &quot;New Model Coming Soon&quot; signage
Responsible (R): Sales Associate
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 10 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1490_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1490_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1490_End10" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1490_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1490_Annotation11">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-259 (ensure controlled execution — Store Daily Management (PA-07.1).) | - operational: Department Supervisor review and approval gate
Owner: Department Supervisor</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1490_Assoc12" sourceRef="W1490_Annotation11" targetRef="W1490_Start5" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1490_Flow13" sourceRef="W1490_Start5" targetRef="W1490_Task6" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1490_Flow14" sourceRef="W1490_Task6" targetRef="W1490_Task7" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1490_Flow15" sourceRef="W1490_Task7" targetRef="W1490_Task8" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1490_Flow16" sourceRef="W1490_Task8" targetRef="W1490_Task9" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1490_Flow17" sourceRef="W1490_Task9" targetRef="W1490_End10" />
    </bpmn:process>
    <bpmndi:BPMNDiagram id="W1490_diag">
      <bpmndi:BPMNPlane id="W1490_plane" bpmnElement="W_W1490">
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1490_Lane1_di" bpmnElement="W1490_Lane1" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="80" width="1160" height="170" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
