    <bpmn:process id="W_W1506" name="W1506. Customer Non-Stock / Special Order Full Lifecycle Management" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Customer requests a product not carried in the store&#x27;s regular assortment (discontinued, specialty item, bulk quantity beyond shelf stock, or custom specification); or Sales Associate identifies unfulfilled customer need during project consultation per W148
Frequency: ~15–25 special orders per store per month
Volume: ~3,000–5,000 special orders/month chain-wide; average order value PHP 8,000–25,000 (higher than regular POS transactions)
Owner: Customer Service Rep
Participants: CSR, Sales Associate, Department Supervisor, Category Manager (HQ), Buyer (HQ), Vendor, Receiving Clerk, Cashier, Customer
Source: workflow W1506 — Customer Non-Stock / Special Order Full Lifecycle Management</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1506_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1506_Lane1" name="Sales Associate">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1506_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1506_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1506_Lane2" name="CSR">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1506_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1506_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1506_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1506_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1506_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1506_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1506_Lane3" name="Receiving Clerk">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1506_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1506_End14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1506_Start5" name="Customer requests a product not carried in the store&#x27;s regular assortment (discontinued…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1506_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1506_Task6" name="Customer request capture">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Customer request capture: Customer approaches Sales Associate or CSR with product request; Associate captures: (a) product description and specifications (dimensions, material, color, brand, model), (b) quantity required, (c) required-by date, (d) customer contact details, (e) whether the item is for a specific project with deadline; Associate searches ERP for existing SKU match (may be discontinued or at another store); if no match found, create Special Order Request (SOR) in system
Responsible (R): Sales Associate / CSR
Accountable (A): Dept Supervisor
Duration: 10–15 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1506_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1506_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1506_Task7" name="Sourcing">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Sourcing: CSR or Department Supervisor identifies potential vendor: (a) check existing vendor master for suppliers of the product category, (b) if new vendor required, initiate expedited vendor creation per MDM-008 (minimum: TIN, contact, payment terms), (c) contact vendor for price quote, lead time, and minimum order quantity; for import items: confirm customs classification, estimated landed cost per FIN-013, and import lead time (45–90 days); (d) if multiple vendors available: select based on price, lead time, and reliability score per W959
Responsible (R): CSR / Category Manager
Accountable (A): Dept Supervisor
Duration: 1–4 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1506_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1506_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1506_Task8" name="Customer quotation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Customer quotation: CSR prepares quotation for customer: (a) item cost + markup (standard special order margin: 35–45%), (b) estimated lead time, (c) payment terms: 50% deposit at order placement (non-refundable), balance at pickup/delivery, (d) cancellation policy: deposit forfeited if vendor has already been ordered; CSR contacts customer with quotation via phone, SMS, or email
Responsible (R): CSR
Accountable (A): Dept Supervisor
Duration: 15–30 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1506_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1506_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1506_Task9" name="Order confirmation &amp; deposit collection">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Order confirmation &amp; deposit collection: Customer accepts quotation: (a) system creates Sales Order with &quot;Special Order&quot; type flag, (b) CSR collects 50% deposit at POS against the special order; deposit linked to Sales Order in ERP, (c) system auto-generates Purchase Requisition routed to Category Manager for approval, (d) Category Manager approves PR and converts to Purchase Order; PO includes: vendor, item description, quantity, required-by date, delivery location (store or DC), (e) customer receives order confirmation SMS/email with SO number and estimated availability date
Responsible (R): CSR / Cashier / Category Manager
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 20–30 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1506_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1506_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1506_Task10" name="PO tracking &amp; vendor follow-up">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: PO tracking &amp; vendor follow-up: CSR monitors PO status weekly: (a) system auto-tracks PO status: Sent → Acknowledged → In Production → Shipped → Received, (b) if vendor misses acknowledged ship date: CSR contacts vendor for update and revised ETA, (c) for import POs: track customs clearance status per PA-02.2, (d) if ETA will miss customer&#x27;s required-by date: CSR contacts customer immediately with revised date and option to cancel per W1133
Responsible (R): CSR
Accountable (A): Category Manager
Duration: 10 min/week per open order</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1506_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1506_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1506_Task11" name="Goods receipt">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Goods receipt: Vendor delivers special order to store: (a) Receiving Clerk processes goods receipt against PO per PUR-011; verifies product matches description, quantity, and condition, (b) for custom or specification-critical items: Department Supervisor performs quality inspection against customer specifications, (c) system updates Sales Order status to &quot;Available for Pickup&quot;; (d) auto-generate customer notification: SMS + email &quot;Your special order is ready for pickup&quot; with store location and 10-day hold period
Responsible (R): Receiving Clerk / Dept Supervisor
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 15–30 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1506_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1506_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1506_Task12" name="Customer pickup &amp; balance payment">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Customer pickup &amp; balance payment: Customer arrives to collect: (a) CSR retrieves item from secure special order staging area, (b) Cashier collects remaining 50% balance at POS, (c) system closes Sales Order, recognizes revenue, (d) for trade accounts: charge to account per W1269 credit terms
Responsible (R): CSR / Cashier
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 10–15 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1506_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1506_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1506_Task13" name="Unclaimed order management">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 8: Unclaimed order management: If customer does not pick up within 10-day hold period: (a) CSR makes 2 reminder calls (Day 5 and Day 8), (b) after Day 10: item disposition options — (i) return to vendor if returnable (vendor return policy permitting per PUR-012), (ii) add to store regular inventory if item fits assortment, (iii) mark down per W93 if close to assortment but slow-moving, (c) deposit handling per W1133 cancellation policy; (d) if item added to regular inventory: deposit credited to store miscellaneous income
Responsible (R): CSR / Dept Supervisor
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 15 min per unclaimed order</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1506_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1506_Flow25</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1506_End14" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1506_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1506_Annotation15">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-259 (ensure controlled execution — Store Daily Management (PA-07.1).) | - operational: transparent lead time communication at quotation (Step 3) and suggesting in-stock alternatives where possible; operational: encouraging customers to bring physical samples or photos for matching
Owner: Customer Service Rep</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1506_Assoc16" sourceRef="W1506_Annotation15" targetRef="W1506_Start5" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1506_Flow17" sourceRef="W1506_Start5" targetRef="W1506_Task6" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1506_Flow18" sourceRef="W1506_Task6" targetRef="W1506_Task7" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1506_Flow19" sourceRef="W1506_Task7" targetRef="W1506_Task8" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1506_Flow20" sourceRef="W1506_Task8" targetRef="W1506_Task9" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1506_Flow21" sourceRef="W1506_Task9" targetRef="W1506_Task10" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1506_Flow22" sourceRef="W1506_Task10" targetRef="W1506_Task11" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1506_Flow23" sourceRef="W1506_Task11" targetRef="W1506_Task12" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1506_Flow24" sourceRef="W1506_Task12" targetRef="W1506_Task13" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1506_Flow25" sourceRef="W1506_Task13" targetRef="W1506_End14" />
    </bpmn:process>
    <bpmndi:BPMNDiagram id="W1506_diag">
      <bpmndi:BPMNPlane id="W1506_plane" bpmnElement="W_W1506">
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1506_Lane1_di" bpmnElement="W1506_Lane1" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="80" width="2000" height="170" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
