    <bpmn:process id="W_W1511" name="W1511. Store-Level Community Engagement, Barangay Relations &amp; Local Partnership Management" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Monthly community engagement calendar; barangay official visit or request; LGU partnership opportunity; community event invitation; store opening in new area
Frequency: ~4–8 community touchpoints per store per month; 1 formal LGU/barangay meeting per quarter per store
Volume: 200 stores × ~6 touchpoints/month = ~1,200 community engagement events/month chain-wide
Owner: Store Manager
Participants: Store Manager, Assistant Store Manager, Sales Associates, Regional Operations Manager, Marketing Manager, HR Manager
Source: workflow W1511 — Store-Level Community Engagement, Barangay Relations &amp; Local Partnership Management</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1511_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1511_Lane1" name="Store Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1511_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1511_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1511_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1511_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1511_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1511_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1511_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1511_Lane2" name="Regional Ops Mgr">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1511_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1511_End12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1511_Start4" name="Monthly community engagement calendar; barangay official visit or request; LGU…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1511_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1511_Task5" name="Barangay relationship maintenance">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Barangay relationship maintenance: Store Manager maintains ongoing relationship with barangay officials: (a) attend barangay council meetings when store-related agenda items arise (business permit, traffic flow, parking, noise complaints, waste disposal), (b) invite barangay captain to store events (grand opening, anniversary, community build), (c) respond to barangay-issued memorandums or directives (clearance sales notifications, community tax certificates, special barangay permits for outdoor events), (d) support barangay initiatives: donate materials for community projects per W1106, sponsor barangay sports leagues or fiestas
Responsible (R): Store Manager
Accountable (A): Regional Ops Mgr
Duration: 2–4 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1511_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1511_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1511_Task6" name="Local partnership development">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Local partnership development: Store Manager identifies and cultivates partnerships with local organizations: (a) local contractors&#x27; association — invite members to trade account program per W1269, offer store tour of new products, host monthly &quot;Contractor Morning&quot; with free coffee and product demos, (b) local hardware stores (smaller competitors) — explore referral partnerships where small hardware stores direct customers to BuildRight for items they don&#x27;t carry (tiles, appliances, power tools) in exchange for reciprocal referrals for small items, (c) local schools and churches — offer bulk material pricing for renovation projects, (d) local real estate developers — establish project supply agreements per W162 for new housing developments in the area
Responsible (R): Store Manager / Sales Associate
Accountable (A): Regional Ops Mgr
Duration: 4–8 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1511_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1511_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1511_Task7" name="Community event participation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Community event participation: Store participates in local community events: (a) LGU-sponsored events: town fiestas, foundation days, trade fairs — set up BuildRight booth with product displays, free project estimation per W148, loyalty program sign-up, (b) community build events: partner with LGU or NGOs for community projects (school repairs, public market renovation) — donate materials per W1106 and provide volunteer labor from store staff, (c) DIY workshops per W147 hosted at the store — open to community members, promote via barangay announcement, (d) store-sponsored events: annual customer appreciation day, free safety seminar for local construction workers
Responsible (R): Store Manager / Sales Associates
Accountable (A): Regional Ops Mgr / Marketing Mgr
Duration: 8–16 hours/event (quarterly)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1511_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1511_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1511_Task8" name="Local permit &amp; regulatory relationship management">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Local permit &amp; regulatory relationship management: Store Manager ensures positive relationship with local regulatory offices: (a) LGU Business Permit and Licensing Office (BPLO): maintain timely renewal per W460, attend any required hearings or inspections, (b) Bureau of Fire Protection (BFP): annual fire safety inspection compliance per W1051, invite BFP to conduct fire safety awareness event at store, (c) local DENR office: ensure environmental compliance per W502 and DOC-007 (hazardous waste), (d) barangay health office: coordinate on pest control per W503 and sanitation standards, (e) local PNP (Philippine National Police): establish direct contact with local police chief for security coordination per W471, report suspicious activities promptly
Responsible (R): Store Manager
Accountable (A): Regional Ops Mgr
Duration: 2–3 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1511_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1511_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1511_Task9" name="Customer loyalty community building">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Customer loyalty community building: Build local customer loyalty through community-centric activities: (a) support local sports teams with BuildRight-sponsored jerseys or equipment, (b) sponsor local job fairs — BuildRight as employer of choice in the community, host recruitment drives per W172, (c) &quot;BuildRight Community Hero&quot; program: recognize local contractors, teachers, or community leaders with special discounts or store recognition, (d) sponsor or participate in barangay disaster preparedness drills — position BuildRight as a resource for emergency construction materials, (e) partner with local TESDA offices for skills training workshops at the store per W600 contractor pipeline development
Responsible (R): Store Manager / HR / Marketing
Accountable (A): Regional Ops Mgr
Duration: 4–8 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1511_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1511_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1511_Task10" name="Community feedback &amp; issue resolution">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Community feedback &amp; issue resolution: Monitor and respond to community feedback: (a) Store Manager listens to community concerns relayed through Sales Associates, security guards, or direct feedback (noise, traffic, drainage, construction debris), (b) resolve issues proactively before they escalate to formal barangay complaints, (c) if community issue cannot be resolved at store level: escalate to Regional Ops Manager with proposed resolution, (d) track community feedback themes monthly and include in store operations review per W575
Responsible (R): Store Manager
Accountable (A): Regional Ops Mgr
Duration: 2–4 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1511_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1511_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1511_Task11" name="Quarterly community engagement review">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Quarterly community engagement review: Regional Ops Manager reviews community engagement effectiveness across stores: (a) store-level community engagement activity log (events attended, partnerships formed, LGU interactions), (b) business permit renewal status — stores with strong community relationships experience faster permit processing, (c) local customer acquisition: % of new loyalty sign-ups attributed to community events, (d) community feedback themes and resolution rate, (e) identify stores needing additional community engagement support (new stores, stores in areas with competitive pressure)
Responsible (R): Regional Ops Mgr
Accountable (A): VP Store Operations
Duration: 4 hours/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1511_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1511_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1511_End12" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1511_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1511_Annotation13">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-259 (ensure controlled execution — Store Daily Management (PA-07.1).) | - operational: quarterly review (Step 7) and standardized engagement calendar; operational: annual community engagement budget per store (PHP 50,000–100,000/year) managed by Regional Ops Manager; operational: tracking loyalty sign-ups, trade account conversions, and sales lift in the period following community events
Owner: Store Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1511_Assoc14" sourceRef="W1511_Annotation13" targetRef="W1511_Start4" associationDirection="None" />
