    <bpmn:process id="W_W5505" name="W5505. Concession Item Catalog, Barcode &amp; Price-Label Onboarding &amp; Governance" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: (a) Concessionaire agreement execution (W177 steps 1–2); (b) new or changed concession item submitted by the concessionaire (new menu item, vending facing change, packaging/size change); (c) barcode change request on an existing concession item; (d) annual catalog reconciliation per agreement
Frequency: ~30–80 new-item requests per month chain-wide plus 1–2 seasonal catalog refreshes per agreement per year; barcode changes occasional (~20–50/month chain-wide); annual reconciliation ~200–600 agreements/year
Volume: ~200–600 active concessionaire agreements carrying typically 25–50 sellable items each (cafe menus, snack counters, vending facing banks; a few large multi-machine operators reach ~200) → ~8,000–15,000 concession SKUs chain-wide (agreement count and catalog size vary inversely: ~40 items/agreement at 200 agreements, ~25 at 600); legacy agreements on the single throughput SKU (W177 step 3) migrate at renewal
Owner: Master Data Manager
Participants: Concessionaire, Store Manager, Merchandising Ops &amp; Master Data (VS-29), Category Manager (adjacency check), IT (portal &amp; label infrastructure), Finance (AR — fee events per W5507)
Source: workflow W5505 — Concession Item Catalog, Barcode &amp; Price-Label Onboarding &amp; Governance</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W5505_LaneSet5">
        <bpmn:lane id="W5505_Lane1" name="Concessionaire">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5505_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5505_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5505_Start6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5505_Lane2" name="Master Data Analyst">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5505_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5505_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5505_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5505_Lane3" name="Store Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5505_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5505_Lane4" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5505_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5505_End14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W5505_Start6" name="(a) Concessionaire agreement execution (W177 steps 1–2); (b) new or changed concession…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5505_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5505_Task7" name="Catalog intake">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Catalog intake: Concessionaire submits items through the concessionaire portal (or a structured file for first load): description, size/UOM, VAT-inclusive opening price, VAT class (food/non-food/service), proposed barcode if any, serving/facing photo; incomplete submissions are returned automatically with the missing fields listed
Responsible (R): Concessionaire
Accountable (A): Master Data Manager
Duration: 5 min/item (portal); 1–2 hrs first-load file</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5505_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5505_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5505_Task8" name="Item-master creation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Item-master creation: Merchandising Ops &amp; Master Data create the record in the concession item namespace with a concessionaire-owner flag and agreement link (W117); the record is distinct from BuildRight-owned SKUs (W252): no cost, no inventory valuation, no replenishment — price and description are concessionaire-controlled fields pending W5506 approval, tax and category flags are BuildRight-controlled; POS-ring behavior and commission calculation (W177 step 4) attach at item level
Responsible (R): Master Data Analyst
Accountable (A): Master Data Manager
Duration: 10 min/item</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5505_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5505_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5505_Task9" name="Barcode governance">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Barcode governance: (a) concessionaire GS1 barcodes are accepted only after a uniqueness check against the full BuildRight barcode space (W311) — a collision with any BuildRight or other concessionaire barcode blocks activation; (b) items without a compliant barcode receive a BuildRight internal barcode from the concession range, following the custom-barcode pattern of W168/W169; (c) a barcode change on an existing item follows the same governance: new code verified unique, old code delinked with an effective date, and a label-reprint task auto-raised (step 4) — the old code stops ringing at the effective cutover, never before the new label is confirmed affixed (sequencing per W5506 step 5)
Responsible (R): Master Data Analyst
Accountable (A): Master Data Manager
Duration: 10–15 min/item; 30 min per collision investigation</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5505_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5505_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5505_Task10" name="Price-label ownership decision">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Price-label ownership decision (recorded on the agreement at setup, per item class): (a) *BuildRight-printed* — concession items join the store label batch cycle (W181 pattern) on BuildRight template/label stock; or (b) *concessionaire-printed* — concessionaire prints on the BuildRight-approved template (item, price incl. VAT, barcode, concessionaire brand) and affixes, with photo confirmation captured in the portal. Shelf-sold items must carry a compliant price tag per RA 7394 (Consumer Act) before any sale; vending-machine face labels follow the machine&#x27;s own label strip but must match the POS price file exactly
Responsible (R): Store Manager / Concessionaire
Accountable (A): Master Data Manager
Duration: 30 min per agreement (decision + template setup)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5505_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5505_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W5505_Task11" name="POS activation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: POS activation: approved items with confirmed labels activate in the price file; central push reaches POS terminals within 60 seconds (continuous price push per the POS architecture); offline terminals apply on reconnect with a stale-price flag
Responsible (R): System / IT
Accountable (A): Master Data Manager
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5505_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5505_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5505_Task12" name="Change &amp; retirement handling">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Change &amp; retirement handling: description/UOM/photo changes follow steps 1–2; item retirement (menu removal, facing exit) deactivates the SKU at a cutover date after the label is confirmed removed; retirements feed the W177 monthly commission reconciliation so removed items stop accruing
Responsible (R): Concessionaire / Master Data Analyst
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 10 min/item</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5505_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5505_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5505_Task13" name="Annual catalog reconciliation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Annual catalog reconciliation: per agreement, Master Data reconciles the active catalog against the agreement scope and the physical floor/machines (with Store Manager); ghost SKUs (agreement-ended items still active) are purged chain-wide — the concessionaire-exit variant runs through W3144-style offboarding and W62 termination where applicable; results feed the W5507 recovery review
Responsible (R): Master Data Analyst / Store Manager
Accountable (A): Master Data Manager
Duration: ~1 hr/agreement/year</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5505_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5505_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W5505_End14" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W5505_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W5505_Annotation15">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-259 (ensure controlled execution — Store Daily Management (PA-07.1).) | - CTL-195 (ensure planogram &amp; price-tag compliance — concession items join the shelf-label price-accuracy audit population) | - operational: barcode uniqueness gate blocks activation on any collision; no sale before confirmed label affixture
Owner: Master Data Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W5505_Assoc16" sourceRef="W5505_Annotation15" targetRef="W5505_Start6" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W5505_Flow17" sourceRef="W5505_Start6" targetRef="W5505_Task7" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W5505_Flow18" sourceRef="W5505_Task7" targetRef="W5505_Task8" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W5505_Flow19" sourceRef="W5505_Task8" targetRef="W5505_Task9" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W5505_Flow20" sourceRef="W5505_Task9" targetRef="W5505_Task10" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W5505_Flow21" sourceRef="W5505_Task10" targetRef="W5505_Task11" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W5505_Flow22" sourceRef="W5505_Task11" targetRef="W5505_Task12" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W5505_Flow23" sourceRef="W5505_Task12" targetRef="W5505_Task13" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W5505_Flow24" sourceRef="W5505_Task13" targetRef="W5505_End14" />
    </bpmn:process>
    <bpmndi:BPMNDiagram id="W5505_diag">
      <bpmndi:BPMNPlane id="W5505_plane" bpmnElement="W_W5505">
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W5505_Lane1_di" bpmnElement="W5505_Lane1" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="80" width="1790" height="170" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
