    <bpmn:process id="W_W5506" name="W5506. Concessionaire Self-Service Price Change Request, Approval &amp; Store-Level Propagation" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Concessionaire submits a price change through the concessionaire portal (cost increase, menu change, promo price, error correction); or requests an emergency rollback
Frequency: ~150–400 price-change requests per month chain-wide (food-input costs, seasonal menus, promo bursts), averaging ~7–10 items per request → ~1,000–4,000 item-level price changes/month
Volume: All ~8,000–15,000 concession SKUs (W5505) are eligible; legacy single-SKU agreements (W177 step 3) are out of scope until migrated
Owner: Pricing Analyst
Participants: Concessionaire (requester), Store Manager (single-store approval), Category Manager (multi-store/chain-wide approval), Stock Associate (label swap), IT (price push), Finance (commission rate unchanged — no role in price decision)
Source: workflow W5506 — Concessionaire Self-Service Price Change Request, Approval &amp; Store-Level Propagation</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W5506_LaneSet7">
        <bpmn:lane id="W5506_Lane1" name="Concessionaire">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5506_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5506_Start8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5506_Lane2" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5506_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5506_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5506_Task14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5506_Task16</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5506_Lane3" name="Store Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5506_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5506_Lane4" name="Stock Associate">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5506_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5506_Lane5" name="Cashier">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5506_Task15</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5506_Lane6" name="Pricing Analyst">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5506_Task17</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5506_End18</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W5506_Start8" name="Concessionaire submits a price change through the concessionaire portal (cost increase…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5506_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5506_Task9" name="Submission">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Submission: Concessionaire drafts the change in the portal: item(s) from the W5505 catalog, new VAT-inclusive price, requested effective date (≥ 3 business days out; same/next-day expedite available per the W5507 fee schedule), and reason code. Drafts have no system effect — the POS price and label stock remain untouched until step 5
Responsible (R): Concessionaire
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 5 min/request</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5506_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5506_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W5506_Task10" name="Automated guardrail validation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Automated guardrail validation (seconds, blocking): (a) within agreement guardrails — max change % per request and absolute floor if agreed in the contract; (b) undercut check — new price more than X% below a comparable BuildRight SKU in the adjacent category flags for Category Manager review (advisory, not blocking); (c) DTI price-freeze check — if the item is on the frozen list (RA 7581, W468), the request is rejected automatically for the freeze duration; (d) VAT math — portal-entered gross price and implied net reconcile to the item&#x27;s VAT class (W5505 step 2). Failed validations return to the concessionaire with reasons; passed requests queue for approval
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5506_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5506_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5506_Task11" name="Approval decision">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Approval decision (SLA: 2 business days, auto-reminder at breach): (a) *single-store items* → Store Manager approves/rejects in the portal (rejection requires a written reason, returned to the concessionaire for rework); (b) *multi-store/chain-wide items* (e.g., a vending operator across 40 stores) → Pricing Analyst endorses, Category Manager approves; (c) *auto-approval* is permitted only when ALL hold: change ≤ ±10%, no barcode/label-format change, item not flagged by the undercut check, requester has no active billing dispute (W5507 step 4). Approval is recorded with approver identity and timestamp
Responsible (R): Store Manager / Pricing Analyst / Category Manager
Accountable (A): Store Manager (single-store) or Category Manager (chain-wide)
Duration: 10 min/manual review; ~40–60% auto-approved</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5506_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5506_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W5506_Task12" name="Scheduling">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Scheduling: on approval the system writes an effective-dated price record to the price master (W289 governance); cutover convention: 06:00 store-local on the effective date (same start-of-business convention as W40 steps 6–8); the old price stays live until cutover
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): Pricing Analyst
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5506_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5506_Flow25</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W5506_Task13" name="Label-first propagation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Label-first propagation (the binding sequence — no step may run early): (a) T-1 day 16:00 — label batch releases: BuildRight-printed items join the store&#x27;s label print batch (W181 pattern); concessionaire-printed items get a portal task due by T-1 close; (b) T-1 close → effective 06:00 — label swap executed and scan-confirmed (handheld scan of the new tag, or portal photo-confirmation with timestamp for concessionaire-printed); (c) effective 06:00 — POS price-file activation pushes within 60 seconds to online terminals; offline terminals defer activation and fly a stale-price flag until reconnect (never applying a price whose label was confirmed but whose push lagged); (d) 05:30 hold rule — if the label swap is NOT confirmed by 05:30 on the effective date for any store, that store&#x27;s activation auto-holds (old price keeps ringing — the customer can never be charged above the posted tag per RA 7394) and the exception escalates to the Store Manager for same-day resolution; (e) vending machines: machine-side price update pushed by the concessionaire operator via telemetry where connected, else manual update with photo confirmation, by the same 05:30 deadline
Responsible (R): Stock Associate / Concessionaire / System
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 15–30 min/store/event (label swap); automated elsewhere</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5506_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5506_Flow26</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W5506_Task14" name="Barcode-change cutover">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Barcode-change cutover: when the price change rides on a barcode change (W5505 step 3c), the new barcode activates in the same 06:00 cutover and only after the new label is confirmed; the old barcode then returns &quot;not found&quot; with a 7-day courtesy alias that rings the new price and alerts the cashier to update the tag
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): Master Data Manager
Duration: Automated (alias monitored)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5506_Flow26</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5506_Flow27</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5506_Task15" name="Post-cutover verification">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Post-cutover verification: W667 daily price verification sweeps concession SKUs on every price-change cutover day (not just random sampling); W69 price compliance audits include concession items in scope; a POS-vs-shelf mismatch triggers immediate re-print per W181 step 5 and, where the customer was charged above the posted tag, the lower-of-two price rule and a goodwill adjustment per W101
Responsible (R): Cashier / Store Manager
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 15 min/day (absorbed in W667)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5506_Flow27</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5506_Flow28</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W5506_Task16" name="Audit trail &amp; settlement feed">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 8: Audit trail &amp; settlement feed: every request retains requester, approver, validation results, timestamps, old/new price, and label-confirmation evidence for 10 years (BIR retention); approved changes feed the W177 monthly commission calculation at the new price from the cutover minute, and changes beyond the free allowance log a fee event to W5507
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): Pricing Analyst
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5506_Flow28</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5506_Flow29</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5506_Task17" name="Emergency rollback">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 9: Emergency rollback: concessionaire or BuildRight may request a same-day rollback of an approved change (pricing error, supplier cost reversal); rollback follows the identical label-first sequence compressed to same-day (print → swap-confirm → activate) with the expedite fee chargeable per W5507; rollback of a price DECREASE may activate immediately (charging less than the posted tag is never an RA 7394 violation) with labels following within 24 hours
Responsible (R): Pricing Analyst / Store Manager
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 1–2 hrs/event</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5506_Flow29</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5506_Flow30</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W5506_End18" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W5506_Flow30</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W5506_Annotation19">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-259 (ensure controlled execution — Store Daily Management (PA-07.1).) | - CTL-241 (ensure controlled execution — Pricing &amp; Promotions (PA-01.2)) | - operational: label-first sequencing with 05:30 activation hold — no POS price activates before confirmed label affixture; freeze-status rejection per W468
Owner: Pricing Analyst</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W5506_Assoc20" sourceRef="W5506_Annotation19" targetRef="W5506_Start8" associationDirection="None" />
