    <bpmn:process id="W_W5507" name="W5507. Concession Service-Fee Billing &amp; Cost Recovery for Labels, Barcode Changes &amp; Admin Services" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: (a) Chargeable service event auto-logged from W5505/W5506 (label print run, barcode change, item add beyond free allowance, expedited or excess price change, custom label stock); (b) monthly concessionaire billing run (W177 step 4)
Frequency: Continuous event logging; ~200–600 concessionaire invoices per month carrying a service-fee section; ~300–800 chargeable events per month chain-wide
Volume: ~5–10% of invoices attract a dispute (~15–50 disputes/month)
Owner: AR Supervisor
Participants: AR Clerk, Concessionaire, Store Manager (first-line dispute), Master Data Analyst (event evidence), Finance (Controller — posting), Legal (fee-schedule enforceability at contracting)
Source: workflow W5507 — Concession Service-Fee Billing &amp; Cost Recovery for Labels, Barcode Changes &amp; Admin Services</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W5507_LaneSet6">
        <bpmn:lane id="W5507_Lane1" name="Legal">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5507_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5507_Start7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5507_Lane2" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5507_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5507_Lane3" name="AR Clerk">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5507_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5507_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5507_Lane4" name="Concessionaire">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5507_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5507_Lane5" name="Finance Analyst">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5507_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5507_End14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W5507_Start7" name="(a) Chargeable service event auto-logged from W5505/W5506 (label print run, barcode…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5507_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5507_Task8" name="Fee-schedule setup at contracting">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Fee-schedule setup at contracting: Legal/Finance record the schedule on the agreement (W177 step 2, W117 record): free allowances (e.g., 1 price change per item per month; 10 item adds per year; standard label stock) and per-event fees (label print per tag; barcode change per SKU; expedited same-day price change per event; excess price change per item; custom label stock at cost + margin; post-exit catalog clean-out). Versioned with effective dates so events bill at the schedule in force on the event date
Responsible (R): Legal / Finance
Accountable (A): Controller
Duration: 1 hr/agreement</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5507_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5507_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W5507_Task9" name="Event capture (no manual billing entry)">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Event capture (no manual billing entry): every chargeable event is auto-logged at source with evidence — item/SKU, requester, portal request ID, approval ID, print-run count, timestamp (from W5505 steps 2–4, 7 and W5506 steps 3, 5, 9); events are provisional until the underlying service completes (e.g., a rejected price change logs no fee)
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): AR Supervisor
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5507_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5507_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5507_Task10" name="Monthly aggregation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Monthly aggregation: the W177 billing run (step 4) gains a &quot;Service Fees&quot; section itemizing events by type with evidence links, alongside Rent + Utilities + Commission; for collection-agent agreements, service fees may instead net against the concessionaire&#x27;s gross sales in the same statement, shown gross-then-net
Responsible (R): AR Clerk
Accountable (A): Controller
Duration: +15 min/agreement/month (on top of W177&#x27;s 30 min)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5507_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5507_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5507_Task11" name="Statement &amp; dispute window">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Statement &amp; dispute window: the concessionaire sees the itemized statement in the portal 5 business days before invoice finalization; disputes are raised in-portal and route first to the Store Manager (operational facts) then Finance (rate/application); resolution adjusts the invoice before posting; an unresolved dispute credits the contested line per W101 and escalates to the agreement-level relationship review (W177) — and an active unresolved dispute suspends that concessionaire&#x27;s auto-approval privilege (W5506 step 3c)
Responsible (R): Concessionaire / Store Manager / AR Clerk
Accountable (A): AR Supervisor
Duration: 20 min per dispute (~15–50/month)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5507_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5507_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5507_Task12" name="Accounting &amp; compliance">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Accounting &amp; compliance: service fees post as service revenue (distinct from rental income and commission income — each carries its own VAT characterization per BIR rules); invoicing follows the BIR e-invoicing path (W473) with 10-year evidence retention; AR posting, aging, and collection follow W8/W108
Responsible (R): AR Clerk / Accountant
Accountable (A): Controller
Duration: 10 min/agreement/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5507_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5507_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5507_Task13" name="Quarterly recovery review">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Quarterly recovery review: Finance compares fee income by event type against actual service cost (label stock &amp; print amortization from W181, Master Data labor hours, expedite overtime); persistent under-recovery triggers a fee-schedule change at renewal (W117) rather than mid-term unilateral increases (contract integrity); results feed the annual catalog reconciliation (W5505 step 7) and agreement profitability view
Responsible (R): Finance Analyst
Accountable (A): Controller
Duration: 2 hrs/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5507_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5507_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W5507_End14" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W5507_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W5507_Annotation15">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-259 (ensure controlled execution — Store Daily Management (PA-07.1).) | - operational: fee-schedule contractual basis enforced by versioned effective dating; provisional event reversal before invoice final; dispute window precedes posting
Owner: AR Supervisor</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W5507_Assoc16" sourceRef="W5507_Annotation15" targetRef="W5507_Start7" associationDirection="None" />
