    <bpmn:process id="W_W5574" name="W5574. Concessionaire Connectivity Request, Approval &amp; Independent-Circuit Governance" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: (a) A concessionaire requests an independent internet circuit for its concession space — at application (W177 step 1), mid-term, or at agreement renewal; (b) a network or facilities review surfaces an unauthorized circuit or self-installed connectivity equipment in a concession space
Frequency: Rare per store — ~0.5–1.5 requests per store per year ≈ 100–300 requests/yr chain-wide across 200 stores; unauthorized-findings intake is event-driven
Volume: ~200–600 active concession agreements (W177); ~100–300 connectivity requests/yr chain-wide at ~0.5–1.5 per store per year; historically ~10–20% of requests clear the eligibility gate (~10–60 approvals/yr chain-wide), building an installed base of a few dozen independent circuits; every agreement carrying one is re-attested annually (step 7)
Owner: Store Manager
Participants: Concessionaire, Facilities Coordinator, Network Engineer (IT Infrastructure), IT Security Manager, Finance (AR), Legal, Concessionaire-Contracted ISP
Source: workflow W5574 — Concessionaire Connectivity Request, Approval &amp; Independent-Circuit Governance</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W5574_LaneSet7">
        <bpmn:lane id="W5574_Lane1" name="Store Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5574_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5574_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5574_Task15</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5574_Start8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5574_Lane2" name="Network Engineer">
