        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5574_Task14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5574_Lane6" name="Finance">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5574_Task16</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5574_End17</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W5574_Start8" name="(a) A concessionaire requests an independent internet circuit for its concession space —…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5574_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5574_Task9" name="Request intake &amp; posture check">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Request intake &amp; posture check: Store Manager logs the request against the agreement (W117) and issues the default-posture notice — connectivity at BuildRight stores is a BuildRight-provided utility recovered in the monthly concessionaire invoice (W177 step 4, W111); an independent circuit is an exception requiring this workflow&#x27;s approvals, and the concessionaire-segmented Wi-Fi alternative on the store&#x27;s own link (W366 step 4) is offered first
Responsible (R): Store Manager
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 30 min/request</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5574_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5574_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5574_Task10" name="Eligibility &amp; need review">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Eligibility &amp; need review: request proceeds only when the bundled service cannot meet a documented requirement — a dedicated payment or ATM link, a connection to a bank or government system mandated for the concessionaire&#x27;s own regulated operations, or bandwidth the store link cannot carry without breaching the W366 QoS floors protecting RF guns and mPOS; convenience or cost alone is not eligibility; ineligible requests are declined with the bundled/segmented alternative documented on the case
Responsible (R): Store Manager / Facilities Coordinator
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 30–60 min/request</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5574_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5574_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5574_Task11" name="Technical isolation review">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Technical isolation review: Network Engineer and IT Security Manager define the isolation envelope — circuit entry via a separate conduit or rise terminated in a concessionaire-owned enclosure; no physical or logical connection to any BuildRight network (corporate LAN, store Wi-Fi, POS/OT zones per W5418); DHCP service confined to the concessionaire&#x27;s own equipment per the W5520 IPAM rules; no BuildRight credentials issued for any circuit-attached device
Responsible (R): Network Engineer / IT Security Manager
Accountable (A): IT Security Manager
Duration: 1 hr/request</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5574_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5574_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5574_Task12" name="Facilities &amp; works approval">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Facilities &amp; works approval: Facilities Coordinator approves the physical route (penetrations, pathway, exterior termination) per W47; exterior works (dish, antenna, façade penetration) additionally require landlord consent where BuildRight is itself a tenant (VS-42/VS-97 master-lease discipline) and LGU permits where applicable; execution only by licensed contractors from the approved list (W47), with a restoration obligation and a restoration holdback retained from the concessionaire&#x27;s deposit
Responsible (R): Facilities Coordinator
Accountable (A): Facilities Coordinator
Duration: 1 hr/request (works 1–2 weeks elapsed)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5574_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5574_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5574_Task13" name="Contract addendum">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Contract addendum: Legal and Finance execute the connectivity addendum to the agreement (recorded on W117): demarcation of responsibility (the circuit, its equipment and its support are exclusively the concessionaire&#x27;s — BuildRight IT is not the helpdesk for it per W48 scope), liability and insurance requirements per VS-147, the restoration duty at exit, and the clause that all concession sales continue to ring on the BuildRight POS throughput SKU (W177 step 3, W5505) regardless of the concessionaire&#x27;s own systems
Responsible (R): Legal / Finance (AR)
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 1–2 hrs/addendum</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5574_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5574_Flow25</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5574_Task14" name="Installation &amp; verification">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Installation &amp; verification: ISP and contractor visits are scheduled under the vendor-representative access procedure (W581) with Store Manager escort per W71; on completion, IT Security verifies the isolation envelope (no crossover, no bridging, DHCP boundary honored) before the agreement&#x27;s independent-circuit flag is set; any network-side accommodation such as a port-isolation rule rides W1409 change control
Responsible (R): IT Security Manager / Store Manager
Accountable (A): IT Security Manager
Duration: 2 hrs/verification</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5574_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5574_Flow26</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5574_Task15" name="Ongoing governance">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Ongoing governance: the independent-circuit flag lives on the agreement record; annual re-attestation rides the concession catalog reconciliation (W5505 step 7) — circuit still installed per the addendum, no crossovers surfaced by discovery (W5520 reconciliation), insurance current; findings suspend the flag pending re-verification
Responsible (R): Store Manager / IT Security Manager
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 15 min/agreement/yr</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5574_Flow26</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5574_Flow27</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5574_Task16" name="Billing adjustment &amp; exit decommissioning">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 8: Billing adjustment &amp; exit decommissioning: Finance removes the internet line from the monthly concessionaire invoice (W177 step 4; W111 allocation) from the addendum&#x27;s effective date; at agreement end (W62) the exit walk-through verifies circuit cancellation by the concessionaire and removal of cabling and equipment before the restoration holdback is released; leftover cabling is removed at concessionaire cost
Responsible (R): Finance (AR) / Store Manager
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 30 min billing adjustment; 1 hr exit walk-through</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5574_Flow27</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5574_Flow28</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W5574_End17" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W5574_Flow28</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W5574_Annotation18">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-259 (ensure controlled execution — Store Daily Management (PA-07.1).) | - operational: no physical or logical crossing into BuildRight networks without IT Security verification; all concession sales continue on the BuildRight POS throughput SKU; restoration holdback released only on exit walk-through sign-off
Owner: Store Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W5574_Assoc19" sourceRef="W5574_Annotation18" targetRef="W5574_Start8" associationDirection="None" />
